PVD("palau_ndp_2023-2026",{"docs":["","Palau NDP 2023 26"],"s":{"1":[[1,"154","6","Government Revenue Generation and Self-Financing Strategy","The PDP and longer-term funding strategy for development expenditure prioritizes the generation of government revenues so that the government may in the future finance its priority investments from its own funds.",""],[1,"154","6","Priority Project Preparation and Feasibility Studies","This will include priority projects of a recurrent nature, such as policy, planning, market research, management and feasibility studies that will help identify revenue-generating development activities.",""]],"2":[[1,"43","3","Cultural and Natural Tourism Product Expansion and Inclusive Marketing","Expanding the number, diversity, and quality of cultural and natural tourism products, equitably marketing tourism products in all communities, and increasing the number of local Palauans able to participate in and benefit from the tourism industry is an immediate priority.",""],[1,"43","3","Rural Tourism Accommodation and Support Services Expansion","Increasing the stock of small tourism accommodations, restaurants, and support services is a medium- to long-term priority in rural communities.",""],[1,"43","4","Tourism Product and Accommodation Expansion","expanding tourism products, accommodations of all types, restaurants, and support services are immediate priorities.",""],[1,"44","4","Cultural and Natural Tourism Product Expansion and Promotion","The number, diversity, and quality of cultural and natural tourism products should be expanded and promoted, and an increasing number of Palauans need to be trained in local tourism, including tourism business management, arts and handicrafts, and customer relations.",""],[1,"59","8","Tourism Product Expansion and Promotion","Increase tourism products, expand promotion, and train Palauans in tourism.",""],[1,"59","8","Tourism Skills Training for Palauans","Increase tourism products, expand promotion, and train Palauans in tourism.",""],[1,"89","6","Sustainable Eco-Tourism and Cultural Use Development","Generate sustainable economic benefits from environmental landscapes, species, and related products, through tourism, sustainable use, and cultural uses",""]],"3":[[1,"32","3","Cultural Site and Tourism Marketing Alignment Initiative","Aligning cultural site programming with tourism marketing is also desired and could build sustainability for maintenance.",""],[1,"32","6","Cultural Site Preservation and Utilization Initiative","Increasing the protection and utilization of cultural sites and practices is a top priority for stakeholders in Koror both to retain culture but also to diversify the economic base.",""],[1,"32","6","Cultural Tourism Diversification Initiative","A priority for Koror and Airai is to diversify tourism to include cultural tourism,",""],[1,"32","6","World Heritage Site Management and Capitalization","in Koror, another priority includes better management of, and capitalization of opportunities associated with the World Heritage Site, which was nominated to the UNESCO convention based on both natural and cultural criteria.",""],[1,"39","7","Sustainable Tourism Promotion","Research, monitoring, and spatial planning, sustainable management of coastal fisheries, growth of aquaculture, expansion of protected areas, more sustainable tourism, and management of diverse habitats will help to preserve and sustainably use marine environments.",""],[1,"43","3","Policies to Limit Foreign Influence in Rural Communities","developing investment, employment, and other policies to limit the impacts of foreign influences remain a medium- to long-term priority in rural communities.",""],[1,"43","4","Foreign Investment Attraction Initiative","Obtaining foreign investment is another immediate priority for Airai and Aimeliik.",""],[1,"126","1","Tourism Regulation and Certification Framework","There are 3 current tourism regulations: (i) the national pandemic safety regulation, (ii) the Boat Owners Association for Tourism, and (iii) tour operator regulations.",""],[1,"126","2","Palau Pledge Responsible Tourism Initiative","Ongoing tourism initiatives are the \"Palau Pledge\"",""],[1,"126","2","Responsible Tourism Education Act","the Responsible Tourism Education Act (restricting the use of plastics and promoting reef-safe sunscreen)",""],[1,"126","2","Pristine Paradise Environmental Fee","the levy of a \"Pristine Paradise\" environmental fee",""],[1,"126","2","Green Fins Programme","and \"Green fins\"",""]],"4":[[1,"126","4","Tourism Statistics and Market Research Support","More detailed tourism statistics are needed to help better understand the impact of tourism on the society and economy of Palau, including its current value-added and to otherwise assist policy planning.",""],[1,"126","4","Commercial Tourism Market Research","International commercial market research is also needed to help Palau better understand what future tourism products and markets could meet the country's tourism goal.",""],[1,"126","4","Regular Tourism Policy Analysis and Advisory Support","Palau could greatly benefit from regular and updated commercial tourism development policy analyses and advice.",""],[1,"126","5","Tourism Data and Impact Assessment Consultancy","this can be carried through as a priority program and project for 2023-2026.",""],[1,"127","5","International Tourism Products and Markets Research and Development Consultancy","Recruitment of international tourism products and markets' research and development consultancy to help define new tourism policy and statistics.",""],[1,"127","7","Intermittent Tourism Policy Planning Adviser Recruitment","Recruitment of an intermittent tourism policy planning adviser.",""],[1,"128","6","Tourism Development Policy","A new Tourism Development Policy endorsed by OEK",""],[1,"128","8","National Tourism Policy and Statistics System","New national Tourism policy and set of statistics.",""],[1,"128","8","Tourism Value-Added Assessment Report","Report on assessment of tourism value- added.",""],[1,"128","13","Tourism Development Policy and Strategy Formulation","The entire private sector is organized and can be engaged in the development of a new tourism development policy and strategy.",""]],"5":[[1,"126","6","Support for Locally Owned Businesses and Small Entrepreneurs","A State Community priority is an outcome of more locally owned businesses and more local small entrepreneurs, i.e., the number of businesses started in Babeldaob and other States other than Koror.",""],[1,"126","6","Basic Infrastructure and Service Standards Development","The BOT could be a lead partner in establishing quality and standards of basic infrastructure and service.",""],[1,"126","7","Small Business Advisory and Assistance Support","The government will continue to advise and otherwise assist small domestic businesses through the Small Business Development Center and the National Development Bank of Palau.",""],[1,"127","8","Infrastructure and Services Standards Development","Establish standards for infrastructure and services.",""],[1,"128","7","Regulatory and Administrative Support for New Legislation","Rules and regulations and regimes of taxation, fees, licenses, permits, and standard operating procedures are all in place to support the new legislation.",""],[1,"128","8","Infrastructure and Services Standards Publication","Published standards for infrastructure and services.",""]],"6":[[1,"32","5","Land Use Planning, Zoning, and Mitigation Measures","Improved governance capacities are also a priority to ensure that economic growth and other forms of development respect Palauan culture, including land use planning, zoning, and mitigation, and policies that limit the impacts of foreign labor on uniquely Palauan communities.",""],[1,"35","3","Integrated Land Management and Sustainable Land Use Planning","Thus, land management in Palau is considered in two categories: 1) Protected areas and 2) Sustainable Land Management (SLM) for all other lands.",""],[1,"35","3","Coordinated Land Use Planning and Habitat Protection","Terrestrial ecosystems and food production habitats can be better preserved through coordinated land use planning, agro-biodiverse food production, water supply protection, and management and protection of terrestrial habitats and resources.",""],[1,"38","3","Land Use Planning and Zoning Implementation","Implementation of land use plans and zoning, via mandated Planning Commissions and State Planning Offices, is an immediate priority.",""],[1,"39","6","Coordinated Land Use and Terrestrial Ecosystem Protection","Terrestrial ecosystems and food production habitats can be better preserved through coordinated land use planning, agro-biodiverse food production, water quality and supply protection, control of key invasive alien species, and management and protection of terrestrial habitats and resources.",""]],"7":[[1,"36","4","Protected Areas Network Support and Expansion","The National Government supports many of these protected areas via a Protected Areas Network (PAN), which has won global innovation awards, and which is a key pipeline to ensure that tourism contributes to environmental protection (via the Pristine Palau Environment Fee/Green Fee and PAN funding).",""],[1,"36","4","Endangered Species Regulation","Palau's biodiversity will be better conserved by endangered species regulation, control of invasive alien species, an increasingly effective Protected Areas Network (PAN), and sustainable tourism practices.",""],[1,"36","4","Invasive Alien Species Control","Palau's biodiversity will be better conserved by endangered species regulation, control of invasive alien species, an increasingly effective Protected Areas Network (PAN), and sustainable tourism practices.",""],[1,"36","4","Sustainable Tourism Practices for Biodiversity Conservation","Palau's biodiversity will be better conserved by endangered species regulation, control of invasive alien species, an increasingly effective Protected Areas Network (PAN), and sustainable tourism practices.",""],[1,"38","3","Protected Areas Expansion and Ranger Compliance Enforcement","The maintenance and growth of protected areas, including the expansion of roles of PAN Rangers to encourage compliance with multiple environmental and cultural laws, is a medium-term priority.",""],[1,"39","7","Protected Areas Expansion","Research, monitoring, and spatial planning, sustainable management of coastal fisheries, growth of aquaculture, expansion of protected areas, more sustainable tourism, and management of diverse habitats will help to preserve and sustainably use marine environments.",""],[1,"39","10","Endangered Species Conservation and Invasive Species Control","Biodiversity will be better conserved by endangered species regulation, control of invasive alien species, an increasingly effective PAN, and sustainable tourism practices.",""],[1,"85","2","Endangered Species Regulations and Species Recovery Plan Implementation","Palau does not yet have national regulations for endangered species, although these are being advanced and when complete will need to be communicated and then enforced, along with the implementation of technical species recovery plans.",""],[1,"85","3","Genetic Diversity Research and Access and Benefit Sharing Support","Understanding of genetic diversity is limited but necessary for Palau to implement its commitments to the convention on biological diversity, maintain agro-biodiversity, and benefit from Access and Benefit Sharing opportunities from the use of genetic data.",""],[1,"86","1","National PAN Strategy and Action Plan Implementation","Palau has a National PAN Strategy and Action Plan but needs resourcing to further implement it, particularly to improve compliance and enforcement in PAN sites and habitat restoration and climate adaptation.",""],[1,"86","1","Protected Areas Management Effectiveness Assessment Update","An update to a 2013-2014 Protected Areas Management Effectiveness (PAME) assessment is underway to measure the status of protected areas.",""],[1,"87","3","National Bird Monitoring and Heritage Conservation Programme","It is the home of the National Bird Monitoring Program and implements research and conservation activities on natural heritage and on links between biodiversity and culture.",""],[1,"88","3","Protected Areas Expansion and PAN Rangers Compliance Enforcement","The maintenance and growth of protected areas, including the expansion of roles of PAN Rangers to encourage compliance with multiple environmental and cultural laws, is a medium-term priority.",""],[1,"88","6","Rock Islands Southern Lagoon Heritage Site Management and Enforcement","In Koror, improving the management of the Rock Islands Southern Lagoon World Heritage Site (RISL) is a priority, with an emphasis on enforcement of the national and state legal framework.",""],[1,"89","9","Protected Areas Management Programme","Protected areas management (enforcement, education, restoration, climate adaptation)",""]],"8":[[1,"149","2","PPP Framework Preparation Support","Subprogram 2 of the policy-based loan from ADB aims to assist the government in preparing a framework for PPP.",""],[1,"149","6","Public-Private Partnership Expansion","The government is considering further PPPs including partnerships in domestic commercial tuna fishing.",""]],"9":[[1,"44","3","Agriculture and Aquaculture Production Expansion","Food security needs to be increased by expanding agriculture and aquaculture production by families, communities, and businesses.",""],[1,"44","3","Food Production Diversification and Market Expansion Support","Diversification of food production, and expansion of the number and types of markets available should also be supported.",""],[1,"59","6","Small-Scale Agriculture and Fisheries Support","Support small-scale agriculture and fisheries.",""],[1,"63","5","Livestock Breeding and Hatchery Support","The BOA supported livestock farmers through the production of piglets and chicks.",""],[1,"63","5","New Livestock Production Facilities","Production capacity and demand for livestock piglets and chicks were steadily increasing and will be supported by new facilities being constructed with the assistance of bilateral partners, but operational support in terms of extension services and facility operations is needed.",""],[1,"63","5","Feed Mill and Affordable Livestock Feed Supply","BOA has a feed mill and manufactures feed which it sells to farmers at cost.",""],[1,"64","4","Low-Cost Tilling and Equipment Rental Service for Farmers","BOA offers this service to farmers at a very low cost, either by directly tilling (approximately 20 acres per year) or by renting equipment at a subsidized cost.",""],[1,"64","4","Expanded Agricultural Extension and Farm Input Support","The growing demand needs increased extension services, additional equipment and supplies to service a growing number of farmers on larger swaths of land.",""],[1,"64","4","Agricultural Water Storage and Irrigation Investment Support","Commercial farms in particular need assistance to invest in infrastructure such as water tanks and irrigation systems.",""],[1,"64","4","Farm Access Road Development","Many of the best soils and agriculture zones need access roads.",""],[1,"66","2","Local Food Production and Consumption Campaign","Continued cross-sector coordination, planning, and implementation (via a comprehensive local food production and consumption campaign), combined with detailed data collection and analysis, is needed to ensure that Palau becomes more food secure across its entire food security spectrum (from production through processing and distribution to consumption).",""],[1,"66","3","Agricultural Capital Investment Facilities","The following major additional capital investments of (i) a post-harvest processing facility, (ii) a swine breeding facility, (iii) a poultry hatching facility, and (iv) a poultry slaughterhouse are all on track to be completed by the end of 2023.",""],[1,"66","4","Taiwan Technical Mission Agricultural Support Services","The Taiwan Technical Mission (TTM) works in close partnership with BOA in providing a range of support services in the fields of livestock, horticultural crops, and aquaculture.",""],[1,"66","4","Palau Community College Cooperative Research and Extension Program","The Palau Community College Cooperative Research and Extension (PCC- CRE) program is part of the US Land Grant System which supports Palau's agricultural sector through its vocational training courses, an agriculture research station, and cooperative extension services.",""],[1,"67","4","Taro Patch Revitalization and Home Garden Support","Revitalization of taro patches in Koror's Rock Islands is a priority for both food security and cultural protection.",""],[1,"69","2","Local Food Production and Consumption Campaign","Comprehensive agriculture and food system planning and coordination and a comprehensive local food production and consumption campaign",""],[1,"69","3","Agricultural Extension and Support Services Expansion","Expansion of agricultural extension and support services in livestock, fruit, and vegetables",""],[1,"69","4","Climate-Resilient Sustainable Community Farming Expansion","Expansion of climate-resilient and culturally and environmentally sustainable farms in communities and increasing production of root crops, vegetables, fruit, and livestock",""],[1,"70","5","Local Food Production Expansion","Doubled local food production to improve food security (accessibility, affordability, and availability) of locally produced livestock, root crops, vegetables, and fruits, with a minimal negative impact on the environment or culture",""],[1,"70","8","Comprehensive Food Systems Strengthening Programme","Comprehensive Food Systems Policy in place Double livestock piglet and chick production (2022-2026) (i) Piggery production 250/year to 400+; (ii) Poultry production 1200 chicks/year to 3000 chicks/year 7,500 square meters of seed bank operational Doubled production of compost (500m3 in 2023 to 1,000m3 facility) Increase vegetable seedling production by 6,000 seedlings/year to 12,000 per year (from 2023 to 2026)",""],[1,"70","8","Land Tillage Expansion and Fruit Sapling Production Programme","Increase land tillage per year by 25%: From 20 acres tilled per year in 2022 to 25 acres tilled per year in FY2027 to 100 acres of new cropland in 4 years. Increase fruit sapling production by 33%: From 1500 fruit trees/hedge species saplings in 2022 to 2,000/year; Decrease fruit fly damage on at least 50 fruit farms.",""],[1,"70","8","Farmer and Food Processor Training Programme","400 trained farmers/food processors (At least 4 training per year targeting 100 farmers per year)",""],[1,"70","8","State Partnership Network for Local Food Production and Marketing","16 State partnerships to produce, consume, or sell local foods (new agriculture zones, construction of markets, construction of roads/water, rehabilitation of productive landscapes, etc.)",""]],"10":[[1,"32","6","Support for Traditional Fisheries and Gleaning Practices","Supporting traditional practices in fisheries and gleaning is a cultural priority in urban areas.",""],[1,"36","2","Domestic Pelagic Fish Production Expansion","Palau has committed to at least tripling local production and consumption of pelagic fish by 2030.",""]],"11":[[1,"9","1","State Master Plan Approval and Consolidation Process","In early 2023 State Master Plans were going through formal approval processes per individual state requirements.",""],[1,"9","1","State Master Plan Coordination and Synthesis","The Palau Governors Association supervised the process of summarizing and collating common themes in State Master Plans for this PDP.",""],[1,"10","12","Rural State Master Planning Initiative","A new, participatory Rural State Master Planning initiative was launched in 2020 through a GEF64-funded project based at the Ministry of Agriculture, Fisheries, and the Environment (MAFE) entitled \"Integrating biodiversity safeguards and conservation into development\" (also known as the Palau Biodiversity Project).","Ministry of Agriculture, Fisheries, and the Environment (MAFE)"],[1,"10","12","Urban and Lagoon Resilience Planning Initiative","Koror began an urban and lagoon resilience planning initiative in early 2022, in partnership with the Great Barrier Reef Foundation, to identify multi-sector development challenges and solutions.",""],[1,"35","1","Land Use Master Plan Development Assistance","need assistance in developing land use master plans that allow for climate change and social and economic development.",""],[1,"35","5","States Master Plan Development and Update Project","The development or update of most States' master plans is ongoing through the GEF 6 project, led by the Ministry of Agriculture, Fisheries, and the Environment.","Ministry of Agriculture, Fisheries, and the Environment"],[1,"39","5","Master Plan and Sustainable Land Use Planning Assistance","The States need additional assistance in developing master plans and sustainable land use plans that allow for climate change and social and economic development.",""]],"12":[[1,"58","21","Climate-Proof Public Water Systems Upgrade and Expansion","Improve, expand, and build new climate-proof Public Water Systems.",""],[1,"86","2","Aquifer Assessment and Sustainable Extraction Study","there is ongoing work to identify and quantify the value of aquifers and to determine recharge processes and sustainable extraction",""],[1,"86","2","Freshwater Source Examination for Outer Islands","Further examination of these water sources is needed, especially on outer islands where there are no streams and where sea level rise poses a threat",""],[1,"86","4","Water Conservation Education and Outreach","education and outreach on water conservation is a minimal first step",""],[1,"88","4","Public Water Source Improvement Program","Improving public water sources is an immediate priority for all communities outside of Koror.",""],[1,"88","4","Water Supply and Distribution System Upgrades","Water systems need improvements along their entire supply and distribution chain, including watershed rehabilitation.",""],[1,"88","4","Watershed Erosion Control and Land Rehabilitation Program","Institutionalizing a program of erosion control, tree planting, or land cover rehabilitation to improve water quality on Babeldaob (for which there is proof of concept) is an immediate priority.",""],[1,"88","4","Outer Islands Aquifer Protection Measures","Improving environmental conditions around aquifers on outer islands is also an immediate priority to protect their extremely limited water supplies.",""],[1,"139","5","Integrated Water Supply and Distribution System Improvement","Water systems need improvements along their entire supply and distribution chain, from watershed rehabilitation to sourcing of new above- and below-ground water sources to improved water treatment to improved and expanded water distribution systems that maintain potable water quality until it reaches the end user.",""],[1,"139","5","Babeldaob Island State Water System Consolidation","On Babeldaob Island, removing the individual burden of water systems from States is a high priority",""],[1,"142","7","Climate-Resilient Potable Water Supply Expansion","The government seeks to provide a climate-resilient, potable water supply that meets new sources of demand.",""],[1,"142","10","Rural Water Pumping Station and Distribution System Rehabilitation","The rehabilitation of rural water pumping stations and distribution systems.",""],[1,"142","11","Rural Water System Expansion","Expansion of rural water systems to new homes and subdivisions.",""],[1,"142","13","Ngerimel Bridge Reconstruction","Re-construction of Ngerimel Bridge which is used by the Koror-Airai Water Treatment Plant personnel to cross to the other side for dams, wells, and transmission lines valves maintenance.",""],[1,"143","3","Peleliu Water Treatment Facility Reconstruction and Reinforcement","Reconstruction and reinforcement of Peleliu Water Treatment concrete walling of the existing 60,000 gallons underground holding tank to avoid further damage to the walling around the underground holding tank.",""],[1,"143","4","Water System Improvement Projects","Various water system improvement projects for Imeong, Ngeremlengui, Mechebechubel, Ngatpang, Mongami & Ngchemiangel Aimeliik.",""],[1,"143","5","Feasibility Study for an Integrated Water System","Feasibility study for the creation of a single, integrated water system for Babeldaob's rural states.",""],[1,"144","18","Feasibility Study for New Centralized Babeldaob Water System","Feasibility study for new, centralized Babeldaob Water System",""],[1,"144","25","Water System Improvement Project","Water system improvement project for Imeong Ngeremlengui, Mechebechubel Ngatpang, Mongami and Ngchemiangel Aimeliik",""],[1,"147","1","Water System Improvement Project","Water system improvement project for Imeong Ngeremlengui, Mechebechubel Ngatpang, Mongami and Ngchemiangel Aimeliik",""],[1,"155","3","Expanded Water Quality Testing Capacity","Expanded water quality testing capacity at EQPB",""],[1,"155","16","Distribution Storage Tank Refurbishment","Refurbish the Distribution Storage Tanks - Airai, Ngermid, Ngerkesoaol, and Ngerkebesang",""],[1,"155","17","Water System Improvement Project","Water system improvement project for Imeong Ngeremlengui, Mechebechubel Ngatpang, Mongami and Ngchemiangel Aimeliik",""],[1,"155","19","Ngerikiil Dam Weir Raising and Dam Wall Reconstruction","Raise Ngerikiil Dam Weir by 2ft and reconstruct Dam Walls",""]],"13":[[1,"140","4","Koror Wastewater Network Interconnection Works","The sewage pump stations' interconnection and network interconnection works are pending.",""],[1,"140","4","Wastewater Treatment Plant Functional Guarantee Testing","Functional guarantee testing is ongoing.",""],[1,"141","2","Subdivision Sewage Treatment Design Requirement","Designing subdivisions to include sewage treatment is an immediate priority.",""],[1,"141","2","Sewer System Construction and Septic Tank Retrofitting","Due to cost, building sewer systems and retrofitting septic tanks is a long-term priority.",""],[1,"142","8","Koror-Airai Sanitation Project Phase II","A second phase of the latter project is planned.",""],[1,"142","9","Koror-Airai System Rehabilitation","The rehabilitation of the Koror-Airai system.",""],[1,"143","10","Rural Sewage Pumping Station and Collection Pipe Rehabilitation","The replacement and rehabilitation of sewage pumping stations and collection pipes in rural areas.",""],[1,"143","11","Technical Planning Support for Septic Tank Suitability","Assistance with technical planning to ensure septic tanks are fit-for-purpose per location/subdivision.",""],[1,"143","12","Feasibility Study for Septic Tank Conversion to Sewage Systems","This will be implemented via a feasibility study for the conversion of septic tanks to sewage systems in rural states and subdivisions.",""],[1,"143","12","Alternative Sewage Disposal Methods Assessment","the government will examine alternative methods of sewage disposal, such as Kubota treatment plants, which are highly efficient and environmentally friendly.",""],[1,"144","28","Melekeok Wastewater Treatment Plant Upgrade","Upgrade of Melekeok Wastewater Treatment Plant with existing capacity and procurement of pumps and spare parts",""],[1,"144","31","Koror Wastewater Pumping Station Refurbishment","Ref: Palau NDP 2023 26 · p.144 · §31\n\nIII. 12 Refurbishment of the 37 Koror wastewater pumping stations.",""]],"14":[[1,"104","3","College of Health Program Revitalization","MHHS is planning to revitalize the College of Health128 program to ensure patient care is not affected while the existing workforce is upskilled, and new health workers are trained.","MHHS"],[1,"104","4","Health Service Performance Assessment and Quality Improvement","Assessing service performance can be done by conducting patient satisfaction surveys, doing walkthroughs of problem areas, and collecting feedback from the staff.",""],[1,"104","4","Revision of Health Policies and Standard Operating Practices","This helps identify quality assurance and improvement gaps that can be addressed by revision of policies and Standard Operating Practices (SOPs), using newer and more efficient methods, and adjusting patient flow by changing the setup of the clinics or other service areas.",""],[1,"105","14","Health System Strengthening Support","JICA support to Bureau of Hospital Service for health system strengthening","Bureau of Hospital Service"],[1,"105","18","Health Systems Strengthening and Service Delivery Improvement","The government is attempting to improve the appropriateness, staffing, management, monitoring, and overall delivery of all health services and to encourage the community to take responsibility for their own health.",""],[1,"106","1","Health System Strengthening","Recently, MHHS has focused on two major short-term objectives (2022-2024) that will help bridge gaps in services and build on efficiencies.",""],[1,"106","1","Health Improvement Framework","Recently, MHHS has focused on two major short-term objectives (2022-2024) that will help bridge gaps in services and build on efficiencies.",""],[1,"106","2","Health Workforce Development","Objective 1 focuses on strengthening 5 strategic areas namely (i) health workforce development,",""],[1,"106","2","Health Information Standards Development","Objective 1 focuses on strengthening 5 strategic areas namely (ii) health information standards and development,",""],[1,"106","2","Health Sector Strategic Planning, Communications, and Reporting","Objective 1 focuses on strengthening 5 strategic areas namely (iii) strategic planning, communications, and reporting,",""],[1,"106","2","Health Standards, Quality Assurance, and Quality Improvement","Objective 1 focuses on strengthening 5 strategic areas namely (v) standards, quality assurance and quality improvement.",""],[1,"107","8","Health Workforce Professional Development and Licensure System","College of Health is developed to oversee professional development initiatives and licensure requirements and ensure minimum core competency standards are completed for 100% of healthcare workers.",""],[1,"107","8","Workforce Wellness Program","Workforce Wellness Program initiated with dedicated staff to ensure program continuity.",""],[1,"107","10","Health Workforce Expansion","The health workforce will expand.",""],[1,"107","13","Continued Prioritization of Health","Administration & OEK will continue to prioritize health.",""]],"15":[[1,"104","5","Health Facility Capital Repair and Rehabilitation","Some of the existing buildings require major capital repairs and rehabilitation to reliably provide health services.",""],[1,"104","5","Health Facility Maintenance and Repair Support","The MHHS carries out building maintenance assisted by the Transportation and Equipment Department and from time to time, the Bureau of Public Works, and local and outside contractors.",""],[1,"104","5","Maintenance Personnel Training Partnership","MHHS partners with Palau Community College to provide training for maintenance personnel to enhance their skills.",""],[1,"105","3","Development of Community Health Centers into Mini Hospitals","The Ministry plans to further develop the main community health centers in Melekeok and Peleliu into mini hospitals.","Ministry"],[1,"105","4","New Public Health and Administration Building","MOH has a 10-year plan to build a new public health and administration building.","MOH"],[1,"105","5","Medical Equipment Replacement and BNH Facility Improvement","Old medical equipment needs to be replaced and improvements made at the current BNH while work is underway for a new hospital.",""],[1,"105","6","BNH Relocation Planning Committee","A committee has been established pursuant to EO 461 and has met multiple times.",""],[1,"105","12","Portable X-Ray Machine Installation","Installation of a portable x-ray machine at Central Community Health Center in Koror",""],[1,"105","15","Transition Unit for Elderly Patients Requiring 24-Hour Care","Transition Unit opening in summer 2023 for elderly patients who require 24-hour care",""],[1,"105","16","Hemodialysis Unit Expansion","Additional 6 hemodialysis units under formal bid process to augment existing 12 units",""],[1,"106","2","BNH Relocation and MHHS Administration Project","Objective 1 focuses on strengthening 5 strategic areas namely (iv) BNH relocation, MHHS administration, and public health building,",""],[1,"106","4","Medical Equipment Replacement and Facility Upgrading","Replacement of other medical equipment including a new incinerator, an energy-efficient lighting system, new plumbing systems, a radio center, major medical equipment, and major general equipment",""],[1,"106","6","New Hospital Construction","Priority Capital Programs are a new hospital at an estimated cost of $120 million",""],[1,"106","6","Public Health Facility Construction","and a new Public Health facility at an estimated cost of $25 million",""],[1,"107","20","Health Facility Equipment and Infrastructure Upgrading","Water cooling system at $500,000, Water sprinkler system at $800,000, Water filtration system at $350,000, Hyperbaric chamber $200,000, Oxygen generation plant $500,000, Medical waste incinerator $40,000, Laundry equipment $25,000, Kitchen equipment $25,000, Laboratory to allow for CLIA certification $100,000, and Cardiac catheterization laboratory $500,000.",""]],"16":[[1,"104","1","National Health Insurance and Medical Savings Account Coverage Scheme","NHI complements MSA by providing coverage for catastrophic illnesses and off-island referrals approved as medically necessary by a Medical Referral Committee established within the MHHS.","MHHS"],[1,"104","1","Public Payment of Health Insurance Premiums for Vulnerable Groups","The government pays the MSA premiums for unemployed senior citizens and the severely disabled using funds earmarked for this purpose from tobacco taxes.",""],[1,"107","10","Health Service Uptake and Cost-Sharing Initiative","Palauans will take ownership of their health by seeking services to improve their health & paying bills.",""]],"17":[[1,"57","9","Labor Policy and Labor Market Development Plan","A new labor policy and labor market development plan could ease private sector activity as well as priority social and political concerns.",""],[1,"58","9","Social Protection Framework Development","build the social protection framework supported by new social, land, and labor policies",""],[1,"75","7","Labor Policy to Improve Salaries and Benefits for Palauans","Labor policy will provide increasingly attractive salary and benefits for Palauans, especially college graduates",""],[1,"93","8","Financial Literacy Program","MOE establishes and implements financial literacy program by FY25.","MOE"]],"18":[[1,"26","7","National Policy on Older Persons","MHHS working with the World Health Organization, community stakeholders, and older persons themselves has developed a National Policy on","MHHS | World Health Organization"],[1,"27","1","10-Year Aging Strategic Plan","Aging supported by a 10-year strategic plan spanning the period 2023-2033.",""],[1,"27","8","Age-Friendly Physical Environment Development","Create age-friendly physical environments through,",""],[1,"27","10","Non-Driving Transportation Options for Older Persons","Transportation options that do not rely on driving to ensure that older persons remain independent and mobile.",""],[1,"27","12","Health System Transformation Across the Life Course","Transform health systems to address individual needs across the life course through,",""],[1,"27","16","Geriatric and Gerontology Workforce Strengthening","Strengthening the geriatric and gerontology workforce to improve the quality of care,",""],[1,"27","17","Primary Health Care Alignment for an Aging Population","Align primary health care to respond to an aging population,",""],[1,"27","18","Healthy Aging Stakeholder Collaboration","Collaborate with public, private, and community stakeholders in support of healthy aging.",""],[1,"27","19","Senior Nutrition Program Expansion","expansion of the existing senior lunch program that serves only Koror to rural communities by partnering with the school lunch program (target date, FY 2025)","MHHS"],[1,"27","19","Senior Medical Transportation Services","develop transportation services for seniors living in Babeldaob for medical appointments and other essential tasks","MHHS"],[1,"27","19","Home Visitation for Older Persons","expansion of home visitation by health workers to aged persons (initiated in FY 2023)","MHHS"],[1,"27","19","Hospital Transition Unit for Seniors","operationalize the transition unit at the hospital for seniors who need continuous care (target, summer of FY 2023)","MHHS"]],"19":[[1,"23","3","Temporary Social Protection Benefit Increase","Palau further increased social protection benefits, albeit on a temporary basis, for both citizens and non-citizens who lost income due to the near cessation of the tourism industry.",""],[1,"24","1","Household Transfer Payments for Crisis Response","Low-income families with children, especially single-parent households, could benefit from an expansion of low-cost childcare options, targeted labor market support to assist parents to prepare for and find work, and transfer payments to help families respond to crises and rise above the poverty line.",""],[1,"24","4","COVID-19 Resilience Support for Poor and Vulnerable Households","In 2020 ADB funded a project to improve the capabilities of poor and vulnerable households to withstand further impacts of COVID-19, from 2021 to 2024.",""],[1,"24","11","Child Subsidy Implementation Regulations","Regulations to implement this legislation are being developed by MHHS.","MHHS"],[1,"26","1","Housing Assistance for Vulnerable Families","housing assistance",""],[1,"26","1","Crisis Transfer Payment Support","transfer payments to help families respond to crises and rise above the poverty line",""],[1,"30","15","Housing Assistance Programme","Provide housing assistance.",""],[1,"153","3","Support for Affected Vulnerable Groups under COVID-19 Response","a $770,000 grant that is currently supporting affected vulnerable groups",""],[1,"153","6","Border Management Support for COVID-19 Recovery and Preparedness","The UNDP also plans to assist Palau, together with Fiji, Samoa, and Vanuatu, with border management in support of COVID-19 recovery and preparedness.",""]],"20":[[1,"5","4","Palauan Culture Awareness Education Programs","the country context focuses on education programs to raise awareness and promote Palauan culture.",""],[1,"5","4","Rural and Outer Islands Cultural Programmes","The rural and outer islands' priorities also focus on offering cultural programs.",""],[1,"5","4","Cultural Site Restoration and Cultural Centers Network","they prioritize the restoration of cultural sites and providing a functioning network of cultural centers.",""],[1,"5","4","Urban Cultural Site and Practice Preservation","Maintaining cultural sites and practices is a priority for urban residents.",""],[1,"18","3","Cultural Education Expansion","The expansion of cultural education is an immediate priority.",""],[1,"18","3","Intergenerational Knowledge Transfer Initiative","A key priority is to transfer knowledge held by elders to youth.",""],[1,"32","2","Community Cultural Programming and Traditional Knowledge Preservation","Investment in regular community cultural programming, with support services to document, communicate, and enable traditional practices is an immediate priority.",""],[1,"32","3","Cultural Site Restoration and Maintenance Programme","Relatively low investment in cultural site restoration programs and ongoing investment into site maintenance needs to be addressed and are immediate priorities.",""],[1,"32","4","Community and Cultural Center Rehabilitation and Accessibility Upgrade","Safe and secure facilities that enable the practice of cultural traditions, and which doubly serve as education centers for the perpetuation of culture, are an immediate priority for communities.",""],[1,"33","5","Cultural Education Programs and Curricula","Design and support delivery of cultural education programs and curricula that emphasize local knowledge, language, traditions, stories, and heritage for young and old.",""],[1,"33","6","Cultural Site Restoration and Maintenance Initiative","Restore and maintain cultural sites to meet local educational and cultural needs while adding value as tourism products.",""],[1,"33","7","Cultural Centers Network Construction and Rehabilitation","Build or repair a network of cultural centers.",""],[1,"33","8","Cultural Site Management Improvement","Improve management of cultural sites in the UNESCO World Heritage site.",""],[1,"37","3","Traditional Knowledge Documentation and Cultural Heritage Protection","Documentation of traditional knowledge, better protection of cultural heritage, raising public awareness of issues facing natural and cultural heritage, and community and professional education and training programs will help perpetuate Palau's close links between cultural and environmental sustainability.",""],[1,"58","15","Cultural Education Programs and Curriculum Development","Design and support delivery of cultural education programs and curriculum.",""],[1,"58","16","Cultural Programming and Curriculum Development","Offer Cultural programming and curriculum.",""],[1,"58","17","Cultural Centers Network Development","Build, retrofit, or equip a network or Cultural Centers.",""],[1,"58","18","Cultural Assets Management in the RISL World Heritage Site","Increase management of cultural assets in the RISL World Heritage site.",""],[1,"60","2","Palauan Cultural Awareness Education Programs","the country context focuses on education programs to raise awareness and promote Palauan culture.",""],[1,"60","2","Rural and Outer Islands Cultural Programmes","The rural and outer islands' priorities also focus on offering cultural programs,",""],[1,"60","2","Cultural Site Restoration and Cultural Centers Network","they also prioritize the restoration of cultural sites and providing a functioning network of cultural centers.",""],[1,"60","2","Urban Cultural Site and Practice Maintenance","Maintaining cultural sites and practices is also a priority for urban residents.",""],[1,"85","3","Cultural Programming Linking Nature and Culture","Many cultural practices are tightly linked to biodiversity, thus support for cultural programming that ties nature to culture is a priority.",""],[1,"87","3","Natural and Cultural Heritage Programming","The Bureau of Cultural and Historical Preservation (BCHP) also contributes to natural and cultural heritage programming.","Bureau of Cultural and Historical Preservation (BCHP)"]],"21":[[1,"100","3","Local Ranger Training and Legal Alignment","Training and alignment of laws are also needed for local Rangers.",""],[1,"101","8","Community Enforcement Capacity Building","Capacity building to improve enforcement capacity in communities",""]],"22":[[1,"150","4","Compact Renewal Grant Assistance","The terms originally specified in the Compact Renewal Agreement were for continuing current grant assistance, although at a declining level.",""],[1,"150","4","CTF Support for Infrastructure Maintenance and Capital Projects","Additional resources were provided to support the CTF, infrastructure maintenance, and capital projects.",""],[1,"151","2","COFA Fund Use Restriction Framework","the new COFA is to be used exclusively for purposes related to education, health, climate adaptation, and the environment, the administration of justice, and public safety or for expenses related to required audits.",""],[1,"151","4","Aid Coordination Unit","The establishment of an Aid Coordination Unit will help the government manage the various donor assistance programs in the interest of national development priorities and coordinate and integrate capital with recurrent budget management.",""],[1,"151","5","Australian Non-ODA Support for Palau","The Government of Australia allocated $4 million per year from 2022 to 2023 in non-ODA funds to support Palau after it graduated from the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development's (OECD) List of Official Development Assistance (ODA).",""],[1,"152","10","Aid Coordination Unit Establishment","The establishment of an Aid Coordination Unit will help the government manage the various development partner assistance programs in the interest of national development priorities and coordinate and integrate capital with recurrent budget management.",""],[1,"154","5","Donor and Development Partner Assistance Alignment","Donor and Development Partner assistance programs are already partially set for the first years of the PDP.",""],[1,"154","6","Negotiated Donor and Development Partner Assistance","Priority development expenditure will otherwise continue to be subject to the negotiation of ongoing donor and development partner assistance programs.",""],[1,"154","7","Aid Coordination and Project Prioritization Mechanism","Future project funding will be coordinated by the new Aid Coordination Unit and all future capital and recurrent expenditure financing will be administered, filtered, scored and ranked in accordance with future budget preparations for each fiscal year.",""]],"23":[[1,"47","2","State-Owned Enterprise Governance Reform Policy","The policy was re-affirmed in 2021.",""],[1,"47","2","State-Owned Enterprise Bill","An SOE bill was drafted in 2022 based on the policy and is pending with the President's office.",""],[1,"47","2","PUC Operational and Regulatory Reform Programme","PPUC underwent a series of operational and regulatory reforms in 2020-2021 linked to an ADB policy- based loan.",""],[1,"47","3","SOE Policy Embedding in Enabling Legislation","The Ministry of Finance intends to embed the policy in its enabling legislation RPPL 9-4, and this will provide the Ministry with the authority to mandate SOE policies.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"47","3","SOE Board Nomination Procedure Reform","Additionally, there is a need for a new board nomination procedure to ensure that the SOE sector operates with qualified directors who possess the necessary skills and experience to effectively oversee the operations of these entities.",""],[1,"49","2","State-Owned Enterprise Reform","As previously mentioned, the government is also continuing reforms to SOEs, including governance legislation and utility reforms.",""]],"24":[[1,"38","1","Environmental Governance Capacity Building and Regulatory Update","Capacity building and extension services, updating of environmental laws, regulations, and policies, and improved awareness and enforcement will improve environmental governance.",""],[1,"38","1","Cross-Sector Environmental Planning Support","Cross-sector planning and updated policy development is increasingly promoted but needs ongoing support.",""],[1,"38","1","Environmental Project Funding Access and Tracking Capacity","Many of Palau's environmental activities are grant supported and funded by donors, thus maintaining capacity to access funds and successful implement and track projects is a key need at every level.",""],[1,"39","14","Sustainable Environmental Financing and Regulatory Strengthening","Conservation and management of Palau's environment can be supported through sustainable financing, updated environmental policies, strategies, and regulations, improved environmental compliance and enforcement, and increased public participation in environmental management.",""],[1,"68","12","Natural Resources Management and Regulatory Update","The government aims to improve overall production and productivity in the sector through better management of Palau's natural resources, review, and update of the existing regulatory",""],[1,"86","4","Watershed Regulation Monitoring and Enforcement","necessitating regular implementation of EQPB's regulations, monitoring, and enforcement","EQPB"],[1,"86","4","Expanded Environmental Surveillance and Permit Enforcement","Continued and expanded surveillance and enforcement are also needed to ensure that development permit conditions are implemented and resources important to human health, livelihoods, or the economy are not harmed",""],[1,"87","3","Environmental Regulations Enforcement","Palau's eight sets of environmental regulations cover every aspect of the environment, with a primary benefit being the protection of water for human and habitat health and are implemented by EQPB.","EQPB"],[1,"88","2","Environmental Legal Framework Updates","Updates to several aspects of the environmental legal framework are needed in the next few years, including updates to the Biosecurity Act and regulations, marine protected area act and regulations, endangered species regulations, marine mammal act regulations; and the PAN Act's enforcement rules and regulations.",""],[1,"89","12","Environmental Law and Regulatory Update","Update environmental laws and regulations",""]],"25":[[1,"86","4","Environmental Laboratory Capacity Expansion","Expanding laboratory capacity to include toxins, chemicals, and minerals in water and soil is needed for Palau to maintain human health as more and more intensive and industrial uses are introduced to Palau's steep and erodible lands",""],[1,"87","2","Cross-Ministry Environmental Coordination and Communications","MAFE's Office of Strategic Support Services (OSSS) coordinates cross-Ministry actions and leads communications to build awareness and environmental stewardship.","MAFE"],[1,"87","2","Food Systems Task Force Secretariat","The OSSS also acts as the Secretariat for the Food Systems Task Force, which is a government-wide body tasked with increasing food security (availability via production as well as affordability, access, and consumption).","MAFE"],[1,"87","2","National Environmental Protection Council Secretariat","The Secretariat for the National Environmental Protection Council (NEPC), a cross-Ministry coordination body, sits in the Ministry of Finance.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"87","2","SDG Measurement Coordination","The NEPC Secretariat also coordinates the measurement of SDGs, including SDGs 2,6, and 11-15, which are directly relevant to the Environment Sector.","NEPC Secretariat"],[1,"87","3","National Spatial Data and Land-Use Analysis System","Spatial data for all of Palau's lands and waters are housed at HE Palau Automated Land and Resources Information System (PALARIS) in the Ministry of Finance.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"87","3","National Hospital Site Suitability Analysis","PALARIS has been tasked with conducting a detailed analysis of suitability for a new national hospital based on social criteria such as access, economic aspects such as cost, and environmental aspects such as water availability and hazardous materials disposal.",""],[1,"89","13","Environmental Communications and Awareness Programme","Environmental communications and awareness programs, including cultural programming and outreach on compliance with laws",""]],"26":[[1,"36","2","Palau National Marine Sanctuary Regulation","The entire EEZ is regulated under the Palau National Marine Sanctuary (PNMS) Act, which established a Domestic Fishing Zone, a closed Marine Protected Area, and an Artisanal Fishing Zone; the act also reconfirmed each State Government's territorial rights from shoreline to 12 nautical miles.",""],[1,"36","2","Sustainable Domestic Pelagic Fishing Support","Support for sustainable domestic pelagic fishing, improved security and enforcement, and expansion of benefit-sharing will protect offshore marine resources.",""],[1,"39","8","Sustainable Domestic Pelagic Fishing Support","Support for increased sustainable domestic pelagic fishing, improved security and enforcement, and expansion of benefit-sharing will protect offshore marine resources.",""]],"27":[[1,"35","4","Aquaculture Expansion and Coastal Marine Resource Management","Palau has committed publicly to at least tripling aquaculture productivity by 2030, which will require careful conversion of nearshore marine areas to productive aquaculture sites.",""],[1,"39","7","Aquaculture Expansion Programme","Research, monitoring, and spatial planning, sustainable management of coastal fisheries, growth of aquaculture, expansion of protected areas, more sustainable tourism, and management of diverse habitats will help to preserve and sustainably use marine environments.",""]],"28":[[1,"95","5","Pelagic Fishery Expansion and Sustainable Nearshore Catch Management","Increasing pelagic fishery production and consumption to shift pressure away from coastal fisheries, and aligning nearshore fishery production with sustainable limits that consider the impacts of climate change are immediate priorities.",""],[1,"96","1","Fishery Data Collection and Stock Assessment System","The development and deployment of consistent data collection protocols and the establishment of Stock Assessments and Harvest Assessments are needed to track fishery production and consumption and to enable adaptive management to be climate resilient.",""],[1,"96","5","Marine Spatial Planning","Marine Spatial Planning (MSP) was underway in 2023.",""],[1,"99","4","Marine Spatial Planning Coordination Mechanism","The MSP exercise for all of Palau's marine waters from shore to the edge of the Exclusive Economic Zone requires sustained and supported coordination among all fishery and aquaculture sector partners.",""],[1,"99","4","Climate Fisheries Research Capacity Expansion","expanding research capacity to develop and track climate shifts and impacts is needed.",""],[1,"100","1","National and State Fishery Policy Reform","investment in new and aligned National and State Fishery Policies is warranted and an immediate need.",""],[1,"100","1","Fishery Spatial Planning and Regulatory Framework","These include spatial plans for specific locations, fisheries regulations on sizes, seasons, gear, licensing, and permitting.",""],[1,"100","1","Marine Protection Act Update and Registration System","An update to the Marine Protection Act and its regulations is underway and should include a registration and permitting system to better generate and track data.",""],[1,"100","1","Fisheries Education and Outreach Programme","Education and outreach are needed to facilitate the uptake of best practices and to encourage compliance with updated laws.",""],[1,"100","2","Nearshore Fisheries Resilience Planning and Regulatory Reform","Priorities include (i) comprehensive planning for commercial and subsistence fishing; (ii) updates to a regulatory regime to usher in changes to seasons and size restrictions, (iii) marine protected areas, and more; an increase in public outreach and engagement with fishers; and (iv) improvement and sophistication of enforcement to encourage compliance with the updated regime.",""],[1,"100","13","Fisheries Policy and Regulatory Framework Review and Update","Undertake a comprehensive review and update and implement fisheries and fisheries- related policy and regulatory framework.",""],[1,"101","1","Fisheries Data Collection and Adaptive Management System","Develop and implement data collection protocols for coastal/nearshore and pelagic fisheries, and for aquaculture, implement monitoring, and create data sharing mechanisms and adaptive management feedback loops, with capacity building",""],[1,"101","2","Fisheries Research and Assessment Programme","Implement research to develop stock and harvest assessments, market studies and goods-and-services value evaluations, sustainable use parameters, and climate projections and adaptation needs for nearshore, offshore, and invertebrate fisheries, including a better understanding of the fisheries markets, their scale, and their main barriers and drivers",""],[1,"101","3","Fisheries Law and Policy Update","Update relevant fishery laws, policies, and best practices, including spatial plans",""],[1,"102","9","Data-Driven Adaptive Management Planning","Increasing the number of plans that use data in adaptive management processes.",""],[1,"102","9","Fishery and Aquaculture Stock Assessment Programme","At least 2 stock assessments (for 1 fishery and 1 aquaculture species by 2026).",""],[1,"102","9","Fishery and Aquaculture Policy Development","New Fishery, Aquaculture Policies by 2026.",""]],"29":[[1,"94","10","Aquaculture and Pelagic Fishery Production Expansion","Palau has committed to tripling aquaculture and pelagic fishery production for local food security by 2030.",""],[1,"98","2","Aquaculture Hatchery and Research Support","the Palau Community College houses the Palau Community College Cooperative Research and Extension Program (PCC-CRE) as a Land Grant System and operates a Multi-Species Hatchery and a Research and Development Station bolstering Palau's capacity in aquaculture.",""],[1,"98","2","Blue Economy Aquaculture Business Development Support","Encouraging more private sector engagement in aquaculture would benefit from the deployment of Blue Economy innovative business models and market development in addition to sustained technical assistance and extension services.",""],[1,"98","6","Mariculture Seed Production Expansion and Decentralization","Continued investment into expansion and decentralization of aquaculture seedling production and training in new species is essential to meet national Blue Prosperity and food security plans.",""],[1,"101","5","Blue Economy Institutional Capacity Building and Training Programme","Build long-term institutional capacity to fill critical \"Blue Economy\" capacity gaps, anticipate emerging needs of the sector, and invest in individuals to effectively lead programs, including investing in extension, capacity building, and training programs for farmers and fishers in fisheries and aquaculture to expand aquaculture production and pelagic fishery production",""],[1,"101","7","Innovative Business Models and Digital Marketplaces for Tuna Fisheries and Aquaculture","Explore innovative business models or digital marketplaces that may involve both government and the private sector to develop domestic tuna fisheries and aquaculture",""],[1,"102","9","Aquaculture Farmer Expansion Programme","Double the number of aquaculture farmers (32 in 2017 to 70 in 2026).",""],[1,"152","5","Palau Mariculture Demonstration Center Renovation","Renovation of Palau Mariculture Demonstration Center",""]],"30":[[1,"39","1","Upland Agriculture and Food Production Diversification","prioritized several short- and medium-term actions to reduce vulnerabilities, such as upland agriculture, diversification of food production, diversification of employment opportunities, and climate-proofing infrastructure.",""],[1,"39","4","Sustainable Agricultural Production Support","Support for tripling of diverse agriculture production in an environmentally and culturally sustainable manner.",""],[1,"64","1","Seed Bank Expansion and Climate-Resilient Water System Investment","The seed bank needs to be extended and investment into water systems is also needed to make it climate resilient.",""],[1,"64","3","Expansion of Compost Production Facilities","BOA produces compost in a small facility. Koror State also produces compost. Neither BOA nor Koror State can keep up with demand, and expansion of compost facilities is needed to further enhance soil quality.",""],[1,"64","5","Invasive Species Control and Monitoring Programme","Persistent control is needed, as is regular research to identify new and emerging biotypes of invasive species and to keep up to date with control methods that will keep them at minimal populations.",""],[1,"64","5","Agricultural Laboratory Operational Support","BOA has a building for a laboratory but needs regular supplies to keep it operational.",""],[1,"66","2","Modernized Online Food Security Monitoring System","Monitoring systems need to be modernized and online, which also requires digital training and maintenance.",""],[1,"66","3","Agricultural Sector Digitization Initiative","Moving toward digitization in the agriculture sector will eliminate the need for a central market.",""],[1,"67","2","Agricultural Sedimentation and Erosion Control Programme","Implementation of best practices in sedimentation and erosion control in agriculture, combined with land use planning and zoning to reduce future sedimentation is an immediate priority.",""],[1,"67","2","Land Cover Rehabilitation and Tree Planting Programme","Institutionalizing a program of erosion control, tree planting, or land cover rehabilitation (for which there is proof of concept) is also an immediate priority.",""],[1,"67","2","Sustainable Food Production Expansion and Extension Services","Expanding food production by opening new leases on land and water is an immediate priority, and identification and extension services to ensure sustainable and culturally relevant practices, especially in traditional agro-forestry, agro-biodiversity, and taro production areas, is another immediate priority.",""],[1,"67","3","Climate-Resilient Agricultural Expansion","Thus, safe, and climate-resilient expansion of agriculture is necessary and an immediate priority.",""],[1,"67","3","Farmer Water Infrastructure Support","Individual farmers need assistance, particularly with water infrastructure to increase the resilience of their farms.",""],[1,"68","5","Government-Wide Food Systems Coordination Mechanism","Taking a more comprehensive food systems approach needs an even larger government-wide coordination mechanism.",""],[1,"69","2","Comprehensive Agriculture and Food System Planning and Coordination","Comprehensive agriculture and food system planning and coordination and a comprehensive local food production and consumption campaign",""],[1,"69","10","Nursery and Compost Facilities Expansion","Expansion of nursery and compost facilities",""],[1,"70","8","Agricultural Production and Purchasing Data System","Data collection to track production and purchasing.",""],[1,"70","27","Compost Facility Capacity Expansion","Double capacity of a compost facility",""],[1,"70","28","Nursery and Greenhouse Expansion with Rainwater Harvesting System","III.4 Expand nursery/greenhouse and rainwater harvesting system",""]],"31":[[1,"67","3","Invasive Alien Species Management Program","Management of invasive alien species (IAS), including control of fruit flies, coconut rhinoceros beetles, and invasive vines, and prevention of new introductions such as brown tree snakes and tilapia, are important for food security.",""],[1,"67","3","Institutionalization of Invasive Alien Species Programs","Institutionalizing existing IAS programs of prevention, awareness, reporting, and control (for which there is also proof of concept) is also an immediate priority for food-productive areas.",""],[1,"69","8","Laboratory and Invasive Species Capacity Expansion","Expansion of laboratory and invasive species capabilities, with increasing invasive species control",""],[1,"88","5","Invasive Alien Species Management and Prevention Program","Management of invasive alien species (IAS), including control of fruit flies, coconut rhinoceros beetles, and invasive vines, and prevention of new priority introductions such as brown tree snakes and tilapia, are important for food security.",""],[1,"88","5","Community-Based IAS Program Institutionalization","Institutionalizing existing community-based IAS programs of prevention, awareness, reporting, and control (for which there is also proof of concept) is also an immediate priority for food-productive areas.",""]],"32":[[1,"71","3","Head Start Early Childhood Education Program","The Head Start program has provided early childhood education in Palau for 56 years.",""],[1,"71","7","Universal and Mandatory Kindergarten Expansion","It will become universal and mandatory for 5-year-olds in SY2023-2024.","MOE"],[1,"72","4","Head Start Community Assessment","In 2023, Head Start is undertaking a community assessment to guide future program directions.",""],[1,"72","4","Head Start Alignment with Ministry of Education","Key issues are harmonizing Head Start with the Ministry of Education specific to year-round schooling and mandatory kindergarten for 5-years olds scheduled to begin in SY2023-2024.","Ministry of Education"],[1,"72","4","Early Head Start Feasibility Exploration","Head Start is further exploring community support for and the feasibility of introducing Early Head Start which provides early learning for children 1-2 years of age.",""],[1,"74","2","Early Head Start Programme","Introduce Early Head Start to provide early learning for children aged 1-2 years.",""],[1,"75","8","Early Childhood Education Teacher Qualification Expansion","Teachers with degrees in early childhood education will increase from 75% (2022) to 100% (2028).",""],[1,"75","8","Early Head Start Expansion for Toddlers","Early Head Start will serve children 1-2 years old.",""],[1,"75","35","Head Start Federal Funding Eligibility Continuation","Palau will continue to be eligible for Head Start Federal funds under new compact.",""]],"33":[[1,"71","6","Elementary School Consolidation in Babeldaob","the MOE consolidated three elementary schools in eastern Babeldaob into one school in 2011 and plans to consolidate the remaining six public elementary schools in northern and western Babeldaob into two schools.","MOE"],[1,"72","1","Relocation of Elementary Schools to Higher Ground","also address the need to relocate three of these elementary schools to higher ground because of climate change and sea level rise.",""],[1,"73","4","K-12 Public School Establishment Task Force","an executive order issued by the Office of the President creating a task force to initiate work on establishing a K-12 public school in Babeldaob","Ministry of Education | Office of the President"],[1,"73","4","Daily Student Busing Service","Since 2009, daily student busing is provided to transport high school students from Babeldaob to and from Palau High School in Koror","Ministry of Education"],[1,"74","9","School Consolidation Review","Explore school consolidation.",""],[1,"75","8","Babeldaob Elementary School Consolidation and Construction","By 2026 construct 4 new elementary schools to consolidate and replace 8 existing elementary schools on Babeldaob.",""],[1,"75","8","Koror School Repair and Replacement Programme","Additionally, 4 schools (3 elementary and 1 high school in Koror) are repaired until they can be replaced with new buildings.",""]],"34":[[1,"72","3","National Scholarship Administration and Overseas Scholarship Support","The Palau National Scholarship Board (PNSB) was established-to provide scholarships to Palauan citizens pursuing higher education in colleges and universities abroad taking into consideration the national objectives and priorities of the Republic of Palau.",""],[1,"72","13","WICHE Membership Acquisition","Gaining membership of the Western Interstate Commission for Higher Education (WICHE)",""],[1,"73","1","Student Recruitment and Scholarship Support for Regional Enrollment","PCC is exploring options for attracting more students from the Federated States of Micronesia (FSM) and the Republic of the Marshall Islands (RMI) by providing travel scholarships, financial aid packages, and a rich educational and cultural experience.",""],[1,"73","1","Online and Hybrid Degree Programme Expansion","PCC is also exploring options to support online or hybrid bachelor's and master's degree programs that will boost enrollment, strengthen partnerships with U.S. Institutions of Higher Education, and deliver a more diverse range of educational opportunities to Palauans.",""],[1,"73","2","Palau National Scholarship Board Student Support Initiatives","PNSB undertakes initiatives to help Palauan students enroll and succeed in post-secondary studies.",""],[1,"73","2","Paid Summer Internship for Returning Students","PNSB has introduced a paid summer internship open to students in their sophomore and junior years of college with the intent of familiarizing them with career opportunities at home.",""],[1,"74","1","Post-Secondary Education Abroad Support and Return Incentives","The PNSB will continue to encourage and support students in preparing for post- secondary education abroad while incentivizing their return to Palau upon graduation.",""],[1,"74","12","Student Enrollment Incentive Packages","Increase enrollment of students from the FSM and RMI by creating incentive packages (e.g., travel scholarships and financial aid packages) that target their specific needs.",""],[1,"74","13","Funding for Online and Hybrid Degree Program Development","Provide funding to support the development of online/hybrid bachelor's and master's degree programs so that critical partnerships with institutes of higher education in the U.S. can be further developed.",""],[1,"75","8","Palau Community College Faculty and Scholarship Support","Improved faculty remuneration and benefits.",""],[1,"75","8","Hybrid Degree Programme Partnership with U.S. Universities","New hybrid bachelor and master's programs introduced in partnership with U.S. Universities.",""]],"35":[[1,"30","6","Disease Preparedness and Surveillance Priority","Disease preparedness and surveillance must also be a priority given the experience of the COVID-19 pandemic and the vulnerability that arises from global transportation.",""]],"36":[[1,"30","10","Government Social Protection Gap-Filling Initiatives","There will be an increasing need to supplement the cultural system with government initiatives to fill gaps in social protection and fulfill the objective of lifting vulnerable persons above the national basic needs poverty line.",""],[1,"31","1","Waste Disposal and Utility Affordability Improvement","Improve waste disposal and affordability of utilities.",""]],"37":[[1,"20","1","Small Business Support and Economic Diversification Initiative","Supporting small business establishments, particularly in key industries that are needed to ensure social protections such as food security, is an immediate priority.",""],[1,"24","1","Low-Cost Childcare Expansion","Low-income families with children, especially single-parent households, could benefit from an expansion of low-cost childcare options, targeted labor market support to assist parents to prepare for and find work, and transfer payments to help families respond to crises and rise above the poverty line.",""],[1,"24","1","Targeted Labor Market Support for Parents","Low-income families with children, especially single-parent households, could benefit from an expansion of low-cost childcare options, targeted labor market support to assist parents to prepare for and find work, and transfer payments to help families respond to crises and rise above the poverty line.",""],[1,"26","1","Low-Cost Childcare Expansion","these families could benefit from an expansion of low-cost childcare options",""],[1,"26","1","Targeted Labor Market Support for Parents","targeted labor market support to assist parents to prepare for and find work",""]],"38":[[1,"24","3","Family Violence Victim Support Services","Victims of family violence, most but not all of whom are women, may need additional support through case management services, access to temporary housing, and access to labor market services.",""]],"39":[[1,"28","12","National Youth Action Plan","The policy is supported by a detailed National Youth Action Plan, which sets out concrete actions to be taken by each sector and agency, along with a framework for monitoring progress toward policy objectives.",""],[1,"29","3","Youth Social Inclusion and Protection Services","Families and communities support the social inclusion of all youth; youth are safe from all forms of violence, abuse, neglect, and exploitation, through robust processes and comprehensive services to support youth who are at risk or who have experienced violence, and supportive families and communities encourage help-seeking; youth in conflict with the law have access to services and facilities to support their rehabilitation.",""]],"40":[[1,"4","5","Performance Monitoring and Financing Framework","The establishment of a Performance Monitoring and Financing Framework, centered on implementation, provides us with a practical tool to confront the challenges hindering Palau's growth and development.",""],[1,"5","1","Institutionalization of Development Plan Processes and Programs","The medium-term outcome in support of that vision is that well-established processes and programs will have been put in place by 2026",""],[1,"6","9","Sector Performance Monitoring and Funding Framework","PDP progress will be annually monitored at the sector level as each sector performance monitoring and funding framework is annually updated every April to May in preparation for budget negotiations.",""],[1,"6","9","End-of-PDP Evaluation","An end-of-PDP evaluation will be prepared and presented",""]],"41":[[1,"51","7","E-Government Expansion Support","MOF plans to further support the expansion of e- government","MOF"],[1,"51","7","Bureau Assessment and Certification Programme","establish an assessment and certification program for each of the bureaus under the Ministry of Finance","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"51","7","Government Staff Ethics Training and Certification Programme","to establish a program for ethical training and certification of government staff",""],[1,"53","7","Public Sector Modernization Program","A long-term program in support of the modernization of the public sector will be needed to continue to assess the system, ensure that HR management is consistent across all Ministries, continue management training, and assess the need for new legislation.",""],[1,"53","7","Ministry Human Resources Structure Review","The Ministry of Human Resources (HR), Culture, Tourism, and Development is reviewing the HR structure of its own Ministry against public service needs.","The Ministry of Human Resources (HR), Culture, Tourism, and Development"],[1,"53","7","Cross-Ministry and State Government Structure Review","Once that review is complete it plans to work with all other Ministries and State Governments to review their structures.",""],[1,"53","7","Public Sector Wage Study","The Ministry of Finance has requested IMF assistance to conduct a wage study.","The Ministry of Finance"],[1,"55","2","Policy Development in Priority Sectors","The government has approved or is developing policies in fiscal and public finance management, non-communicable diseases, tourism, culture, youth, aging, and public sector human resources management.",""],[1,"55","2","New Policy Development for Economic and Social Sectors","Further, new policies in economic development, land, labor, private sector development, social protection, agriculture, and fisheries are needed to help achieve development outputs and outcomes.",""],[1,"55","4","Permanent Government Policy Planning Institution","A permanent institution of central and state government policy planning is therefore needed to ensure that national and sector plan priorities are identified for funding and to facilitate the coordination and formulation of new policies in support of growth and development.",""],[1,"55","5","Central Economic Planning Office and Aid Coordination Office","MOF plans to establish a central economic planning office that will include an Aid Coordination Office and be responsible for the continued assessment of macroeconomic performance, the strengthened assessment of all sector development, and the assessment of economic feasibility including recurrent cost implications of all investment projects, proposed PPPs, and other capital expenditure including that of the SOEs.","MOF"],[1,"55","5","Future Aid Coordination and Partner Engagement","The PDP will be presented to Palau's donors and development partners as well as all domestic development partners to garner support for stronger, future aid coordination.",""],[1,"56","4","Central Statistical Data Collection System","The government has adopted a policy not to burden the private sector with requests for statistics but to adopt a central collection point for each of the major economic categories of information.",""],[1,"56","4","Public Sector Financial Reporting Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening the capacity of state governments and other units of the general government to provide timely and adequate financial statements would support the compilation of fiscal data at the general government level.",""],[1,"56","5","National Statistics Production and Survey Programme","The Office of Budget and Planning will continue to conduct a population census every ten years, a household income and expenditure survey every 5 years, and develop a series of quarterly economic statistics.","Office of Budget and Planning"],[1,"57","4","National Development Planning Structure Reform","The Office of the President is developing a new structure for national development planning.","The Office of the President"],[1,"57","6","Donor and Development Partner Coordination Mechanism","Donor and development partner development programs could be better coordinated in the interest of Palau's development.",""],[1,"57","12","Permanent Central Government Policy Planning Institution","A permanent institution of central government policy planning will help facilitate the formulation of new policies in support of growth and development.",""],[1,"59","12","Public Sector Productivity Improvement Strategy","Design and implement strategies to improve public sector productivity.",""],[1,"74","8","Performance Metrics and Reporting Guidelines Development","Develop performance metrics and reporting guidelines.",""]],"42":[[1,"113","6","Telecommunications Competition and Universal Service Reform","Regulation that encourages fair competition on a commercial basis for the improvement of telecommunications services for all of Palau and encourages expansion via a revitalized Universal Service Obligation (USO) process.",""],[1,"114","1","Regulatory and Legislative Reform for the Communications Sector","Re-framing of regulations and legislation to accommodate the dynamic changes in the sector e.g., where attention is monetized by \"over the top\", often global, providers who make no contribution to the costs of local networks or to local tax revenues.",""],[1,"114","2","Telecommunications Infrastructure Investment Incentive Reform","Creating a legal and regulatory environment that encourages investment in critical telecommunications infrastructure.",""],[1,"114","3","Tax Removal on Consumer Telecommunications Equipment","Supporting equitable conditions for the adoption of technology and innovation in Palau for all citizens regardless of their socio-economic status, through the removal of all taxation on the import and sale of consumer telecommunications equipment.",""],[1,"115","7","Universal Service Obligation Enforcement and Nationwide Coverage Expansion","The law on USO is enforced and nationwide coverage is delivered through a sustainable 'Play or Pay' approach to ensure access for all Palauans.",""],[1,"115","10","Universal Service Obligation Enforcement","USO enforced.",""],[1,"155","10","Fiber-Optic Cable Expansion","Expansion of fiber -optic cable",""]],"43":[[1,"77","1","Power Grid Reinforcement and Smart Meter Deployment","The transmission network will need to be extended to solar and wind power plants and reinforced to accept power from the proposed IPP- owned power plants.",""],[1,"78","7","Second 34.5 kV Transmission Circuit Between Aimeliik and Malakal","A second 34.5 kV circuit is required between these two generating stations.",""],[1,"79","2","Transmission Network Expansion and Reinforcement for Renewable and IPP Power Integration","The transmission network will need to be extended to the selected location of solar and wind power plants and reinforced to accept power from the proposed IPP-owned power plants.",""],[1,"79","5","Electricity Distribution Network Rehabilitation and Automation","Capital investments will be required over the next ten years to reconstruct the aged distribution lines, relocate lines to the shoulders of paved roads, and apply automated reclosers.",""],[1,"79","5","Distribution Line Extensions for Small-Scale Generation Connection","The 13.8 kV lines will also require some minor extensions to allow connection of small-scale generation, including a land-fill site generation facility.",""],[1,"80","5","Transmission Network Upgrade","Upgrade transmission network (Table 18).",""],[1,"80","6","34.5 kV Transmission Line Construction for IPP Connection","Ene-2 34.5 kV line construction to connect IPPs: Must be implemented, otherwise, Solar IPP cannot be operational even though the PV power plant is constructed.",""],[1,"80","7","34.5 kV Transmission Line Construction","o Ene-1 34.5 kV line construction to improve system stability:",""],[1,"80","8","Battery Energy Storage and Energy Management System Installation","The project will install a minimum 15 MW/15 MWh BESS",""],[1,"80","9","Grid Protection System Upgrade","Protection systems to reduce the frequent blackouts of the grid system will be installed.",""],[1,"81","2","Electric Vehicle Charging Infrastructure Expansion","· Enhance Electric Vehicle (EV) charging infrastructure.",""],[1,"81","3","Power Utility Capacity-Building for Smart Grid and Electric Mobility Management","Their capacity to manage new power systems and electric mobility infrastructure will be improved.",""],[1,"81","6","34.5kV Line Construction to Connect IPPs","34.5kV line construction to connect IPPs",""],[1,"81","7","34.5 kV Transmission Line Construction","34.5kV line construction to improve system stability",""],[1,"81","8","13.8kV Line Reconstruction","Reconstruction of 13.8kV lines",""],[1,"81","10","Rehabilitation of 34.5/13.8 kV Stations","Rehabilitate all existing stations and provide 34.5 kV circuit breakers.",""],[1,"81","12","Smart Meter Replacement Programme","Replace existing meters with smart meters.",""],[1,"81","13","Underground or Insulated Power Line Replacement Feasibility Study","In future fiscal years, PPUC will also consider the feasibility of replacing existing overhead lines with underground or heavily insulated transmission and distribution power lines, particularly in urban areas where it is difficult to maintain adequate clearances from structures.",""],[1,"83","8","Electricity Transmission Network Upgrade","Upgraded transmission network by FY24.",""],[1,"83","8","Electricity Distribution Line Expansion","New distribution lines completed by FY26.",""],[1,"83","8","Smart Meter Installation Programme","New smart meters installed by FY24.",""],[1,"83","14","Feasibility Study for Underground Power Lines in Urban Areas","Feasibility study of replacing existing overhead lines with underground in urban areas",""],[1,"83","15","Grid Code Establishment","II.2 Establish grid code.",""],[1,"83","19","Transmission Network Upgrade","III.2 Upgrade transmission network.",""],[1,"83","27","Grid-Forming Battery Installation near Koror","Installation of a grid forming battery near Koror",""],[1,"155","5","Sustainable Power Infrastructure Investment Program","Sustainable investment program for power generation, transmission, and distribution",""],[1,"155","12","SCADA Software System Upgrade","Update SCADA software system",""],[1,"155","21","High-Speed Data Recorder Installation for Fault Analysis","Installation of high-speed data recorders for fault analysis",""],[1,"155","23","Grid-Forming Battery Installation near Koror","Installation of a grid forming battery near Koror",""]],"44":[[1,"34","5","National Climate Change Adaptation and Mitigation Response","National climate change responses are focused on adaptation, mitigation, and disaster risk management.",""],[1,"34","5","Cross-Sector Climate Change Mainstreaming in Sector Plans","Priority Climate change strategies for natural environments and human settlements and infrastructure are included directly and indirectly across several other PDP sector plans including Energy, Housing, Water and Sanitation, Transportation, Environment, Agriculture, and Fisheries sector plans.",""],[1,"34","5","Climate Adaptation Planning and Renewable Energy Transition","Ongoing adaptation and planning for climate change are national and sub-national priorities and include strategic planning and adaptation measures, improved access to climate-related financial assistance, and transition to renewable energy sources.",""],[1,"39","2","Climate Change Adaptation and Planning Measures","Ongoing adaptation and planning for climate change include strategic planning and adaptation measures, improved access to climate-related financial assistance, mitigation through a transition to renewable energy sources, energy efficiency, and waste reduction, disaster risk reduction and preparedness, and identification and servicing of vulnerable peoples.",""]],"45":[[1,"39","11","Integrated Waste Management and Pollution Control Services","Improved waste management services, segregation, composting, and recycling, landfill operations for improved hazardous waste and oil spill management, contaminated site management, rehabilitation of closed dumps, and chemical tracking, monitoring, and reporting will help reduce pollution of lagoon waters and prevent disease and other public health issues.",""]],"46":[[1,"36","3","Catchment Management and Watershed Protection","Catchment management and protection, freshwater monitoring and supply management, and freshwater lake and estuarine habitat protection will help to preserve Palau's freshwater environment.",""],[1,"36","3","Freshwater Monitoring and Supply Management","Catchment management and protection, freshwater monitoring and supply management, and freshwater lake and estuarine habitat protection will help to preserve Palau's freshwater environment.",""],[1,"36","3","Freshwater Habitat Protection","Catchment management and protection, freshwater monitoring and supply management, and freshwater lake and estuarine habitat protection will help to preserve Palau's freshwater environment.",""],[1,"39","9","Freshwater Catchment Management and Protection","Freshwater catchment management and protection, freshwater monitoring and supply management, freshwater lake and estuarine habitat protection, and management of the cumulative impacts of sewage and septic tanks will help preserve the freshwater environment.",""],[1,"39","9","Freshwater Monitoring and Supply Management","Freshwater catchment management and protection, freshwater monitoring and supply management, freshwater lake and estuarine habitat protection, and management of the cumulative impacts of sewage and septic tanks will help preserve the freshwater environment.",""],[1,"39","9","Freshwater Lake and Estuarine Habitat Protection","Freshwater lake and estuarine habitat protection, and management of the cumulative impacts of sewage and septic tanks will help preserve the freshwater environment.",""],[1,"39","9","Sewage and Septic Tank Impact Management","management of the cumulative impacts of sewage and septic tanks will help preserve the freshwater environment.",""],[1,"39","12","Safe Water Supply Improvement","Improved access to safe water supplies, improved sanitation programs and sustainable, climate-proof construction will help protect community health and the environment.",""],[1,"39","12","Sanitation Program Improvement","Improved access to safe water supplies, improved sanitation programs and sustainable, climate-proof construction will help protect community health and the environment.",""]],"47":[[1,"12","3","State-Owned Enterprise and Public Finance Reform","Reformed State-Owned Enterprises (SOEs), civil service pension fund, social security, and State Government finances.",""],[1,"12","3","Land and Labor Policy Reform","New land and labor policies are implemented.",""],[1,"20","3","Government Labor Policy Statement","A government statement of labor policy would help clarify future employment needs, associated education and training requirements, the government's position on immigration, support for new labor standards, and labor rights, and better direct the required labor market legislation and regulations.",""],[1,"30","4","Government Labor Policy Statement","A government statement of labor policy would help clarify future employment needs, associated education and training requirements, the government's position on immigration, support for new labor standards, and labor rights, and better direct the required labor market legislation and regulations.",""],[1,"32","5","Policies to Limit the Impacts of Foreign Labor","Improved governance capacities are also a priority to ensure that economic growth and other forms of development respect Palauan culture, including land use planning, zoning, and mitigation, and policies that limit the impacts of foreign labor on uniquely Palauan communities.",""],[1,"32","5","Palauan-Led Growth Legal and Policy Reform","Investment in fair and equitable legal and policy development that encourages Palauan-led growth (such as mandates for citizen-led tourism or leasing) is a medium-term priority.",""]],"48":[[1,"18","4","Capacity Building and Training for Rural and Outer Island Governments","Rural and Outer Island State Governments have prioritized capacity building and training in social and economic sectors for government employees and residents to improve the effectiveness of governance and improve economic conditions.",""]],"49":[[1,"21","1","Gender Mainstreaming Policy Implementation","The Palau National Gender Mainstreaming Policy is a key policy document that calls for the integration of gender considerations into policies and programs",""],[1,"21","3","Gender Mainstreaming Accountability and Sex-Disaggregated Data System","The Palau National Gender Mainstreaming Policy advocates for an accountability mechanism supported by the production of sex-disaggregated data and gender indicators that can be used to monitor the impacts of programs and services on women and men and to use in closing gender gaps when appropriate.",""]],"50":[[1,"29","17","Climate-Proof Health Facility Investment and Hospital Relocation","The National Infrastructure and Investment Plan41 identifies a need for new investment in climate-proofing health facilities with a priority for the relocation of the national hospital and certain low-lying community health centers.",""],[1,"29","17","School Relocation, Consolidation, and Renovation Investment","Likewise, the Ministry of Education has identified new investments needed to relocate low-lying schools, consolidate inefficient small schools in Babeldaob, and renovate schools in Koror.","Ministry of Education"],[1,"30","7","Relocation of Health Facilities to Higher Ground","There is a need to relocate the national hospital and several community health centers in low-lying areas to higher ground to ensure the long-term sustainability of services.",""],[1,"30","9","Climate-Resilient Education Infrastructure Investment","There is also a need to invest in new education infrastructure to counter the effects of climate change and increase efficiencies in school management.",""]],"51":[[1,"29","17","Accessibility Upgrades for Public Infrastructure","In addition, there may be a need to adjust or improve existing infrastructure to consider emerging needs related to access by persons with disabilities and senior citizens.",""]],"52":[[1,"30","2","Rural and Outer Island Housing Subdivision Investment","The immediate priority to meet the needs of the most vulnerable, while also building a sense of community, is to invest in housing subdivisions on public lands.",""],[1,"30","2","Rural Infrastructure and Community Amenities Upgrade","Investment into subdivision and engineering design, infrastructure (roads, power, water, sewer, storm drainage, waste management, etc.), community amenities (parks, community centers, sidewalks), and safety features (e.g., streetlights) is the most pressing immediate priority for communities outside of Koror.",""],[1,"30","13","Rural and Outer Island Population Retention and Housing Access Initiative","Grow the population of rural and outer island communities by actively recruiting and encouraging Palauans to move \"home\" by streamlining the housing subdivision process, easing the burden of building a home, and increasing the amount and diversity of subdivision lots and affordable homes available.",""],[1,"30","14","Community Design and Neighborhood Support Services","Strengthen a sense of place by conducting community design and planning and offering support services to create neighborhoods that include increasing access to goods and services, a growing number of childcare options, recreational opportunities, and community educational programming.",""],[1,"38","4","Controlled Migration to Upland Housing Subdivisions","controlled migration to upland housing subdivisions is an immediate priority",""],[1,"38","4","Climate-Resilient Engineering Design Support","engineering designs that minimize risks of subdivisions and other developments are needed",""],[1,"38","4","Technical Planning and Analytical Capacity Expansion","Increasing access to technical planning and analytical expertise is an immediate priority",""]],"53":[[1,"35","2","Fiscal Buffer Building and Contingent Disaster Financing","It has therefore been building fiscal buffers and securing contingent financial assistance from the Asian Development Bank (ADB) to help finance the required future adjustments.",""],[1,"38","5","At-Risk Infrastructure Elevation, Reconstruction, and Rehabilitation","Elevation, reconstruction, or rehabilitation of these at-risk investments is a medium- to long-term priority.",""],[1,"38","5","Outer Islands Critical Infrastructure Improvement","in outer islands, improving key infrastructure such as water systems, transportation, safety systems, and communications is an immediate priority.",""],[1,"38","5","Solar System Installation and Building Code Development for Disaster Risk Reduction","Reducing disaster risk through the installation of solar systems and the development of building codes is a long-term priority.",""],[1,"39","1","Climate-Proofing Infrastructure","prioritized several short- and medium-term actions to reduce vulnerabilities, such as upland agriculture, diversification of food production, diversification of employment opportunities, and climate-proofing infrastructure.",""],[1,"39","1","Reliable and Safe Outer Islands Transport Access","For outer islands, having access to reliable, affordable, and safe transportation is also essential.",""],[1,"39","3","Climate-Resilient Infrastructure Investment","Improve future climate resilience in the existing stock and future investments in infrastructure.",""],[1,"39","12","Climate-Proof Construction Initiative","Improved access to safe water supplies, improved sanitation programs and sustainable, climate-proof construction will help protect community health and the environment.",""]],"54":[[1,"39","7","Marine Environment Research, Monitoring, and Spatial Planning","Research, monitoring, and spatial planning, sustainable management of coastal fisheries, growth of aquaculture, expansion of protected areas, more sustainable tourism, and management of diverse habitats will help to preserve and sustainably use marine environments.",""],[1,"39","7","Sustainable Coastal Fisheries Management","Research, monitoring, and spatial planning, sustainable management of coastal fisheries, growth of aquaculture, expansion of protected areas, more sustainable tourism, and management of diverse habitats will help to preserve and sustainably use marine environments.",""],[1,"39","7","Habitat Management for Marine Conservation","Research, monitoring, and spatial planning, sustainable management of coastal fisheries, growth of aquaculture, expansion of protected areas, more sustainable tourism, and management of diverse habitats will help to preserve and sustainably use marine environments.",""]],"55":[[1,"40","1","Economic and Structural Reform Program","The government has already committed to a wide-ranging program of economic and structural reform, and this will help secure government finances and strengthen the economy.",""],[1,"42","6","Fiscal Discipline and Revenue Collection Reform","the economic growth strategy will be complemented by the recovery and expansion of government revenues through continued fiscal discipline, more efficient revenue collection, and SOE, social security, and pension reforms",""],[1,"42","7","Fiscal Reform Package","The government continues to implement fiscal reforms including the adoption of a Fiscal Responsibility Framework in 2018, a business profits tax in 2022, the introduction of a goods and services tax in January 2023 (a value-added tax), reforms to the wages and hotel occupancy taxes, and reforms to revenue administration.",""],[1,"43","7","Prudent Fiscal Policy and Revenue Mobilization Reform","the economic growth strategy will be complemented by the recovery and expansion of government revenues through continued prudent fiscal policy, more efficient revenue collection, and SOE, social security, and pension reforms to reduce if not eliminate demands for government subsidies.",""],[1,"44","1","Revenue Mobilization for Fiscal Buffers and Trust Fund Capitalization","The government also needs to generate increased revenues to fund priority fiscal buffers for natural disasters and climate change, to further capitalize the trust fund, and restructure the economy.",""],[1,"53","8","Public Finance Management Roadmap","The PEFA will be followed by the preparation of a Public Finance Management roadmap to be implemented by the government over the period of the PDP.",""],[1,"54","1","Economic and Fiscal Update Reporting","The Ministry of Finance (MOF) also started to produce Economic and Fiscal Updates to underpin the budget and operationalized Medium-Term Fiscal Strategy Guidelines (29 June 2022).","Ministry of Finance (MOF)"],[1,"54","1","Social Security Reform Bill Preparation","The government has also supported the preparation of a social security reform bill.",""],[1,"54","1","Public Finance Management Strengthening Support","ADB and PFTAC are assisting the government to strengthen its public finance management.",""],[1,"54","2","Pension Reform to Defined Contribution Plan","finalize pension reform by switching to a Defined Contribution Plan by FY 24",""],[1,"54","2","Internal Auditor and Controller General Position Creation","create a position for an Internal Auditor/ Controller General",""],[1,"54","2","Debt Management System Establishment","establish a debt management system in FY24 costing an estimated $3 million",""],[1,"59","7","Public Finance Reform","Continue to reform all public finances to stem losses, raise revenues, reduce debt, and coordinate aid.",""],[1,"59","10","Fiscal Buffer and Trust Fund Financing","Fund fiscal buffers and the trust fund.",""],[1,"92","6","Pension System Sustainability Reforms","Government policy is to implement reforms to ensure longevity and sustainability.",""]],"56":[[1,"43","1","State Master Plan Implementation Support","An immediate priority is to enable the implementation of State Master Plans, which include economic development objectives, climate resiliency objectives, and collective benefit principles, through the creation of new positions for State Planners60 which can coordinate, implement, and track master plans.",""],[1,"43","1","State Planning Commission Support and Participation Mechanism","Achieving participatory input and buy-in from a supported and funded State Planning Commission is another immediate priority.",""],[1,"46","3","National and State Development Planning Alignment","An important challenge for all the states is the need to strengthen planning and align national and state development objectives and budgets.",""],[1,"54","3","Local Governance Strengthening Project","The joint pilot partnership, the Local Governance Strengthening Project (LGSP), has provided the space for collaborative work between the MOF, Office of the Public Auditor, five pilot states, and the Ministry of State to engage within the local government sector to identify gaps and to develop diagnostic tools to strengthen local governance.","Ministry of State | MOF | Office of the Public Auditor"],[1,"54","3","Public Finance Management Standard Operating Procedures","One of the successful diagnostic tools identified is the development and adoption of the state government's public finance management standard operating procedures (PFM SOP) to enhance capacities surrounding management, documentation, and reporting of fiscal and public assets and resources towards consistent and sustainable delivery of public goods and services.",""],[1,"54","3","Public Participation and Civic Engagement Initiative","In addition, increased public participation and engagement in policy development through increasing public awareness of the individual and collective civic responsibility prescribed by the Palau Constitution as well as their respective state government Constitutions.",""],[1,"54","4","Expansion of Local Governance Diagnostic Tools","The Ministry of State has utilized the joint pilot partnership towards developing content and contextualized diagnostic tools to strengthen local governance at the state government level and is now seeking the resources to expand and extend the diagnostic tools to benefit the remaining eleven state governments outside of the LGSP.","Ministry of State"],[1,"55","7","State Planning Capacity and Commission Support","Hiring state planners and funding state planning commissions is an immediate priority.",""],[1,"55","7","Inclusive Planning Commission Participation","Empowering representation and participation, particularly from traditional leaders and community groups, through planning commissions is another immediate priority.",""],[1,"55","7","Multi-State Spatial and Land Planning Technical Support","Ensuring multi-state spatial and land planning technical support",""],[1,"56","1","Spatial Data Support and Regional Planning Strengthening","services, such as spatial data support as provided by PALARIS79 and regional and cross-border planning, is another immediate priority.",""],[1,"56","1","State-National and Community Partnership Coordination","Building on partnerships between state governments and the national government, as well as between communities and NGO partners, remains a priority that can be achieved through dedicated state planners and regional planning bodies, and associated technical assistance.",""],[1,"56","2","State Government Technical Assistance Capacity Support","This can be accomplished by financing and enabling access to technical assistance in engineering, planning, financial analysis, Environmental Impact Statements, CIP planning, and scenario planning.",""],[1,"56","3","Empower Representative Planning Commissions","empowering representative planning commissions is an immediate priority",""],[1,"56","3","Strengthen Traditional and Elected Leader Engagement Forums","Communities want to strengthen ties between traditional and elected leaders and engage traditional leaders more deeply in governance, by providing forums and decision-point opportunities",""],[1,"56","3","Improve Government Communications and Transparency","Improving communications and transparency, including by taking advantage of new communications mediums and the Internet, is a medium- to long-term priority",""],[1,"56","3","Construct Modern State Offices","Building new, modern state offices is a long-term priority for some communities",""],[1,"57","11","Technical Assistance for State Government Financial Management","Further technical assistance would help strengthen the management of State government finances.",""],[1,"57","11","National-State Development Planning Alignment","An important challenge for all the states is to strengthen planning and align national and state development objectives and budgets.",""],[1,"58","1","State Planning Capacity and Participatory Planning Commission Strengthening","State planners need to be hired and representative and participatory planning commissions empowered and resourced to implement state master plans, land use plans, and zoning codes.",""],[1,"58","2","Regional Planning Services through Central Planning Office","Multi-state, cross-border, and state-to-national coordination should be strengthened by providing regional planning services (via a central planning office under PNCA 31).",""],[1,"58","3","Long-term Support for PALARIS-Based Communities","Multi-state and spatial planning needs support by securing long-term assistance for communities based at PALARIS.",""],[1,"58","4","Technical Expertise Support for Community Planning and Investment","Access to technical expertise in engineering, planning, financial analysis, Environmental Impact Statements, CIP planning, and scenario planning should be provided through annual financing, or the provision of personnel dedicated to community needs.",""],[1,"59","13","Master and Land Use Planning, Zoning, and CIP Coordination","Enable, implement, and coordinate Master and Land Use Plans, Zoning, and CIP.",""],[1,"59","15","State Planning Strengthening","Continue, support, and strengthen State planning.",""],[1,"59","16","Participatory Planning and Government-Wide Policy Formulation Reform","Adopt participatory planning and strengthen government-wide public policy formulation.",""],[1,"59","17","Technical Planning and Engineering Capacity Support","Stabilize and increase access to technical planning, engineering, and analytical expertise.",""],[1,"88","3","Land Use Plan and Zoning Implementation","Implementation of land use plans and zoning, via mandated Planning Commissions and State Planning Offices, is an immediate priority, included in the Governance Pillar.",""],[1,"89","10","Community and Sector Land Use Planning Support","Community and sector land use planning, including spatial analyses and technical assistance",""]],"57":[[1,"49","2","Private Sector Investment Climate Reform","The government is continuing reforms to improve the environment for private sector investment including foreign direct investment.",""],[1,"49","2","Secured Transactions Law and Online Registry","Palau has introduced secured transactions law and an online registry.",""],[1,"49","2","Credit Register Assessment","The Government with ADB PSDI support is currently assessing the possibility of introducing a credit register that will assist with reviewing credit applications.",""],[1,"49","2","Domestic Arbitration Policy and Law Development","The government has started policy work on a domestic arbitration policy and law.",""],[1,"49","2","Electronic Registry Development for Corporations Law","The Ministry of Finance commenced implementation of the new Corporations Law by developing technical specifications to establish a new electronic registry.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"49","2","Online Registry Implementation","The implementation of the online registry will commence in March 2023.",""],[1,"49","2","Public-Private Partnership Policy Framework","The President issued an executive order effective 3 September 2021 that formalized a policy statement for Public-Private Partnerships (PPPs).",""],[1,"49","2","PPP Selection, Monitoring, and Regulation Procedures","This statement helps minimize contingent liabilities from PPPs with procedures guiding the selection, monitoring, and regulation of private sector partners and transactions.",""],[1,"49","2","PPP Transparency Procedure","It is complemented by a parallel PPP transparency procedure, mandating the disclosure of key terms and conditions for prospective transactions, to strengthen market confidence and promote competition.",""],[1,"50","1","Investment Promotion Development Unit","The Ministries of Finance (MOF), Human Resources, Culture, Tourism and Development, and Public Infrastructure and Industries plan to jointly create a Development Unit for investment promotion.","Ministries of Finance (MOF), Human Resources, Culture, Tourism and Development, and Public Infrastructure and Industries"],[1,"50","2","Private Sector Policy Improvement Strategy","The government will work with representatives of the private sector, including foreign investors, to list, detail, and prioritize remaining issues of concern, and then to jointly work through these issues with a view to gradually adopting improved policies.",""],[1,"57","7","Private Sector Development Strategy","A private sector development strategy will help improve the environment for investment, commerce, and trade.",""],[1,"92","4","Secured Transaction Registry","Secured Transaction Registry - enacted and in place",""],[1,"92","4","New Corporations Act Implementation","New Corporations Act - enacted and in the process of being implemented",""],[1,"92","4","Private Bank and Trust Bank Legislation","Private Bank and Trust Bank Legislation - enacted, not implemented",""],[1,"92","9","Financial Sector Macro System Improvements","Macro System Improvements - Development of components for the financial sector, expansion of oversight to all financial institutions, and upgrade capacity with government and regulators.",""],[1,"93","5","Financial Sector Legislation for a Safer and More Equitable Environment","Legislation is passed that creates a safer and more equitable financial environment.",""],[1,"93","8","Financial Sector Protection Legislation","Legislation passed for the protection of land, bankruptcy, and consumer credit protection by end of FY25.",""]],"58":[[1,"43","2","State Government Training and Private Enterprise Pipeline Development","communities would like to develop training programs and pipelines that would create more efficient State Governments and would move trained state personnel into private enterprise.",""],[1,"43","2","Private Enterprise Support Package for Rural Communities","State Governments and NGO partners can support the development of private enterprise through a suite of actions, ranging from the creation of markets (physical and literal), more secure land and aquaculture leases, construction of food processing centers, and facilitation of support services such as business planning and loan application help for the most vulnerable community members.",""],[1,"43","2","Expanded Small Entrepreneur Support Services","Expanding the state's capacity to offer these support services to small entrepreneurs, especially those in food production, is an immediate priority.",""],[1,"44","2","Small Business and Entrepreneurial Support Capacity Strengthening","The capacity of State Governments and partners should be strengthened to provide small business and entrepreneurial support, particularly in the food production sectors.",""],[1,"49","3","Private Enterprise Development Support Package","state governments and NGO partners aim to support the development of private enterprise through a suite of actions, ranging from the creation of markets (physical and literal), more secure land and aquaculture leases, construction of food processing centers, and support services such as business planning",""],[1,"50","1","Small Business Advisory and Financial Assistance","The Small Business Development Center and the National Development Bank of Palau will continue to provide advisory and financial assistance to small businesses.",""],[1,"59","3","Private Sector Enabling Environment Improvement","Improve private sector productivity by improving the environment for private sector activity.",""],[1,"59","5","Small Business and Entrepreneurship Support","Support small businesses and entrepreneurship.",""],[1,"59","14","Private Sector Growth Strategy","Design and implement a strategy to promote the growth of the private sector.",""],[1,"92","5","Stablecoin Pilot for Financial Inclusion","Palau is implementing a Stablecoin pilot to improve financial inclusion and access.",""],[1,"93","8","Financial Services Access Expansion","Improve access to finance and financial services (ongoing).",""]],"59":[[1,"42","8","Rural Housing Stock Expansion and Amenities Improvement","Thus, the expansion of housing stock and improvement of amenities is the most immediate priority for rural states.",""],[1,"50","6","Expansion of State Public Land Lease Programs","Thus, the expansion of lease programs is a medium-term priority for most States.",""],[1,"51","2","Land and Housing Policy Review and Drafting Process","Further study of land and housing issues and practices is required with a focus on how to strengthen land ownership and use, possibly with a further focus on drafting a new policy through extensive consultations.",""],[1,"57","8","New Land Policy","A new land policy could facilitate private investment and economic development as well as urban development planning and help to further protect Palauan ownership.",""]],"60":[[1,"43","6","Agriculture and Fisheries Commercial Investment and Development Policies","New agriculture and fisheries commercial investment and development policies are needed to support diversified growth and development.",""],[1,"59","7","Agriculture and Fisheries Commercial Investment Policies","New Agriculture and Fisheries commercial investment policies.",""],[1,"65","7","Digital Marketplace for Food System Sales","Modernizing sales and investing in a digital marketplace, with ongoing digital support, is a priority across the entire food system.",""],[1,"66","1","Organic Certification Support for Women-Owned Taro Farms","This work is being advanced by NGOs with assistance from BOA.","BOA"],[1,"66","3","Support for Existing Roadside Markets","Existing roadside markets have provided an avenue for small-scale producers.",""],[1,"68","9","Farmer Training and Commercialization Support","The BOA with other partner agencies is training and encouraging farmers to increase production and commercialize farming operations","BOA | other partner agencies"],[1,"69","5","Technical Support for Root Crop Commercialization and Diversification","Provision of technical support to commercialize and diversify root crop processing",""],[1,"69","6","Online Marketing Mechanism Development","Development of an online marketing mechanism",""],[1,"70","8","Root Crop Packing and Processing Expansion","Expand root crop packing and processing from taro to include tapioca and breadfruit (production of flour, chips, new products, etc.) (1 crop, 1 product to 3 crops, at least 6 products)",""],[1,"70","8","Online Agricultural Marketing System","Online marketing system operational with reduced food waste and stable supply and demand pricing",""],[1,"70","21","Organic Certification Program","Organic Certification Program operational (Funded through NGO partners)",""]],"61":[[1,"51","6","Increase Police Presence and Ranger Enforcement Capacity","an immediate need is to increase police presence, or expand the enforcement capacity of Rangers, to deter such crimes.",""],[1,"58","6","Strengthen Police Presence and Ranger Enforcement Capacity","The police presence (through MOJ and/or local deputies) and enforcement capacity of Rangers need to be strengthened in all communities.","MOJ"],[1,"59","20","Police Presence and Ranger Enforcement Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen police presence and increase Ranger enforcement capacity.",""]],"62":[[1,"45","1","Community Outreach Expansion Program","MOF has a program to expand community outreach.","MOF"],[1,"59","16","National Unity Programs","Programs to unify Palau.",""]],"63":[[1,"45","4","Annual State Block Grant Transfers","The national government provides annual state block grants to each of the 16 states for operational and capital improvement projects.",""],[1,"46","3","State Expenditure Efficiency Technical Support","Continued funding by the National Government budget process, and continued access to technical services to improve the efficiency of State expenditures, is an immediate priority.",""]],"64":[[1,"58","9","Education Quality Renewal Program","Programs to renew the quality of education",""],[1,"72","5","Education System Modernization Initiatives","Substantial funding support has been invested to modernize the Palau education system by implementing the following initiatives:","Ministry of Education"],[1,"72","6","Textbook Acquisition","Acquiring new textbooks",""],[1,"72","8","Teacher Professional Development and Continuing Education","Supporting teacher professional development and continuing education",""],[1,"72","9","School Curriculum Review and Update","· Reviewing and updating the school curriculum",""],[1,"72","10","Year-Round School Year Implementation","Implementing year-round school year",""],[1,"72","11","Automated Student Information System","Implementing an automated Student Information System",""],[1,"72","12","Public School Accreditation through WASC","Accrediting all public schools through the Western Association of Schools and Colleges (WASC)",""],[1,"72","14","Special, Adult, and Career and Technical Education Programs","Implementing special education, adult education, and career and technical education programs with federal funding support",""],[1,"72","15","Daily Student Transportation and Meal Support","Providing daily student busing, breakfast, and lunch",""],[1,"74","3","Recurrent Education Sector Operating Expenditure","Continued recurrent expenditure of $9.4 million per annum to fund teachers, administration, and other staffing, staff running costs, school and headquarter running costs, maintenance, and repairs.",""],[1,"74","4","Curriculum Review and Revision","Conduct curriculum review and revision.",""],[1,"74","5","Palauan Studies Strengthening Initiative","Strengthen Palauan studies (teaching of history, values, language, and culture).",""],[1,"74","6","Financial Literacy Integration Across Curriculum","Integrate financial literacy across all content areas.",""],[1,"74","7","Parental Engagement Program Formalization","Formalize parental engagement program.",""],[1,"74","10","School Facilities Upgrade Programme","Upgrade school facilities including repair and replacement of buildings.",""],[1,"74","11","Faculty Compensation Improvement","Improve salary and benefits packages for highly qualified faculty.",""],[1,"74","14","Teacher and School Principal Remuneration Improvement","Improve teacher and school principal remuneration and benefits.",""],[1,"74","15","School Leadership Training Program","Establish a school leadership training program.",""],[1,"74","16","Expanded Learning Pathways and Advanced Placement Option","Increase learning pathways including the introduction of an Advance Placement option.",""],[1,"74","17","Instructional Strategy Improvement for Diverse Learners","Improve instructional strategies to meet the needs of diverse learners.",""],[1,"75","5","Inclusive and Quality Education and Training Services","Inclusive and quality education and training services are provided for all students",""],[1,"75","8","Teacher Qualification Upgrade and Parent Partnership Strengthening","Strengthen MOE and parental partnerships as measured using parent portals for student grades, monthly parent meetings with MOE leadership, and resulting survey results.","Ministry of Education"],[1,"75","8","Technology-Enabled Curriculum Personalization","Improve educational curriculum by utilizing technology to enable more individualized instruction in all academic core classes in all grade levels.",""],[1,"75","8","CAL Implementation in English and Math Classes","Implement the systems of CAL in all English and Math classes in all grades from K-12.",""],[1,"75","8","School Rehabilitation and Replacement Programme","School buildings are repaired or replaced to provide an optimum learning environment.",""]],"65":[[1,"58","9","NCD and Mental Health Response Program","resolve NCDs and mental health disorders",""]],"66":[[1,"58","20","Disaster and Climate Change Adaptation and Mitigation Program","Programs to adapt, mitigate, and manage disasters and climate change, and enforce environment policies.",""],[1,"59","1","Natural Resource Policy Development","Draft new natural resource policies.",""],[1,"59","1","Climate-Resilient Infrastructure Adaptation","Adapt infrastructure for climate change.",""],[1,"87","2","Climate Change Policy and Action Plan Update","OCC is updating the Palau Climate Change Policy and Action Plan, which will identify climate adaptation, mitigation, and disaster response needs for 2024-2034.","Office of Climate Change"],[1,"87","2","Climate Change Projections Update","OCC, NEMO, and the National Weather Office to update climate change projections that will then feed into the updated sector and land use plans.","Office of Climate Change | National Emergency Management Office | National Weather Office"],[1,"88","1","Climate-Resilient Building Code Development","Palau does not have Building Codes, which need to be climate resilient and low emission to meet our stated climate commitments.",""],[1,"88","1","Climate-Resilient Infrastructure Upgrade Programme","Necessary climate-resilient upgrades to infrastructure have been identified in relevant sectors.",""]],"67":[[1,"59","2","Erosion and Sedimentation Control and Land Cover Restoration","Institutionalize erosion and sedimentation control and restore land cover.",""],[1,"59","2","Integrated Land, Freshwater, and Marine Planning","Continue land, freshwater, and marine planning for climate change and development.",""],[1,"70","8","Land Rehabilitation and Erosion Control Programme","Reduced area of land that is actively eroding and/or facing invasive species threats (Baseline 2019: 12,500 ha actively eroding; GEF6 Project Document).",""],[1,"84","4","Palau Forest Action Plan","A Palau Forest Action Plan108 is being implemented.",""],[1,"85","1","Sustainable Forest Management Policy Endorsement and Implementation","The Policy needs to be endorsed and implemented.",""],[1,"86","2","Forest and Landcover Restoration and Fire Prevention","Forest and landcover restoration and rehabilitation, combined with fire prevention and other threat abatements, is needed for highly erodible areas and needs to be done in partnership with communities",""],[1,"88","1","National Nursery Operations Expansion","In the environment sector, continued and expanded operations of the national nursery are needed to maintain and increase forestry and food security efforts to rehabilitate land and reduce climate vulnerabilities across multiple sectors.",""],[1,"89","4","Forest Cover Maintenance and Expansion Support","State governments maintain and increase forest cover with national, technical, and financial support (Palau PAN and other funding mechanisms)",""],[1,"89","7","Forest, Mangrove, and Land Ecosystem Restoration and Erosion Control Programme","Forest, mangrove, and land research, planning, ecosystem restoration, landcover rehabilitation, and erosion control, and expanded nursery operations",""]],"68":[[1,"85","3","Invasive Alien Species Prevention and Control Measures","Invasive alien species pose a threat to Palau's native biodiversity, including agro- biodiversity, and require research and assessment, prevention, control, and eradication measures, consistent public and targeted outreach, and technical planning.",""],[1,"85","3","Invasive Species Protection Operations","Research is underway at the Palau Community College (PCC-CRE). Continued and expanded operations of invasive species protection, including preparation of species response plans and procedures are needed.",""],[1,"89","11","Threat Abatement and Species Response Planning","Threat abatement, including invasive species prevention, control, and eradication where possible, development of species response plans, and fire prevention",""],[1,"89","14","Environmental and Species Law Monitoring and Enforcement","Monitoring, surveillance, and enforcement of environmental and species laws, regulations, and permit conditions, including expanded capacity to monitor via laboratory capacity",""]],"69":[[1,"76","3","Electricity Infrastructure Maintenance and Development Program","PPUC's investment program references the maintenance and development of the future of electricity, including the implementation of renewable electricity.",""],[1,"76","4","Backup Energy Source for Grid Stability","This will require a backup energy source to provide fast-speed frequency and voltage regulation, either in the form of battery storage and, or diesel generation.",""],[1,"76","5","Renewable Energy Sector Investment Expansion","Furthermore, there are calls for investment in the renewable energy sector, in recognition of Palau's potential as an energy exporter, including offshore wind power plants and the subsequent requirement of adoption of technologies that are new to the Palau electricity grid, as well as the upgrading, reinforcement, and construction of transmission lines.",""],[1,"76","5","Offshore Floating Solar Pilot Testing","Offshore PV solar plant installations floating on the ocean are currently being tested.",""],[1,"76","5","Offshore Energy Development Initiative","The development of offshore energy has the potential to deliver sustainable energy resources and the development of offshore wind is highlighted in PPUC's investment plan.",""],[1,"78","1","Independent Power Producer Electricity Generation Contracts","PPUC could contract out a large fraction of the electricity generation to independent power producers (IPPs) through long-term power purchase contracts, at prices significantly lower than the cost of electricity generation through a diesel generating plant.",""],[1,"78","4","Renewable Electricity Generation Procurement from Independent Power Producers","Electricity generation from renewables can be contracted out to IPPs",""],[1,"78","4","Diesel Backup Generator Replacement Investment","a part of the diesel generating plant, required as a backup energy source, will still require investment to replace generators as they reach the end of their service life",""],[1,"79","11","Tariff Reform for PPUC Sustainability","Policy priorities are (i) tariff reforms to introduce market-driven incentives to enhance PPUC's sustainability",""],[1,"79","11","Private Investment Mobilization for Renewable Energy","and (ii) leveraging private investments to meet the country's renewable energy target.",""],[1,"79","11","PPUC Financial Recovery Plan","The government has approved PPUC's financial recovery plan, which aims to restore liquidity and profitability.",""],[1,"80","1","Renewable Energy Scale-Up and Tariff Reform","management, reform its tariffs, and scale up renewable energy generation.",""],[1,"80","2","Electricity Tariff Adjustment and Renewable Energy Expansion","The energy sector will move to financial and economic self-sufficiency over the PDP period through (i) gradually increasing electricity tariffs to secure PPUC financial solvency, and (ii) increasing the supply of lower-cost energy through the installation of renewable energies.",""],[1,"80","3","Diesel Generating Plant Replacement and Generator Overhaul","The replacement of the diesel generating plant at the end of its service life with the larger generators requiring overhaul over the next 5 years.",""],[1,"80","4","Replacement and Rehabilitation of Existing Diesel Generating Stations","Ene-5 Replacement and Rehabilitation of existing diesel generating stations: Since all diesel generation plants in the Koror-Babeldaob power system have not undergone proper and timely maintenance, there is a risk that a breakdown of the plants might occur at any time.",""],[1,"82","1","Renewable Energy Transition and Grid Upgrade","For power generation, transmission, and distribution as well as renewable energy and energy efficiency, Palau has a goal of being 100% Renewable by 2035.",""],[1,"83","8","Electricity Tariff Adjustment for Viable Operations","Tariff increases provide for viable operations by FY25.",""],[1,"83","8","Renewable Energy Investment Expansion","Private investments in renewable energy with 45% of total energy supplied by renewables by FY25.",""],[1,"83","8","Diesel Generating Plant Replacement","Replacement of the diesel-generating plant in FY24.",""],[1,"83","28","Legislative Support for Tariff Increase","Legislature support for increased tariffs to enable a sustainable system.",""],[1,"83","29","Private Sector Renewable Energy Investment","The private Sector continues to invest in renewables.",""]],"70":[[1,"79","10","Human Resources Management Framework for PPUC","The overarching challenge is to unify the organization within a comprehensive human resources management framework and discontinue the use of public service practices.",""],[1,"79","10","Expansion of PPUC Office Accommodation","There is also a need to expand office accommodation, possibly on a new site.",""],[1,"81","13","Public Utility Office Accommodation Construction","New office accommodation at an estimated cost of $5,000,000, this amount includes possible land acquisition and construction.",""],[1,"81","14","Sustainable Investment Program","Sustainable Investment Program (ADB's TA)105",""],[1,"92","10","NDBP New Building Construction","NDBP requires a new building as it expands its services and client base.",""]],"71":[[1,"50","1","E-Commerce and FinTech Development Support","MOF also plans to support the further development of e-commerce and FinTech.","MOF"],[1,"92","4","Digital Residency Act","Digital Residency Act - enacted and implemented",""],[1,"92","5","Digital Residency Program","The Digital Residency program is modeled after that of Estonia.",""],[1,"93","8","Financial Sector Technology Adoption","Increased use of technology in financial services (ongoing).",""]],"72":[[1,"93","17","New Technology for Financial Access","Increase the use of new technology for improved financial access.",""],[1,"93","19","Financial Literacy Programs for Schools, Individuals, and SMEs","Develop and implement financial literacy programs for schools, individuals, and SMEs.",""],[1,"93","22","Technology Solutions Research and Implementation","Research and implement technology solutions with assistance of ADB, IMF and WB",""],[1,"93","23","Regulatory and Technical Support for Fintech Solutions","Provide regulatory and technical support for the implementation of Fintech solutions",""],[1,"93","24","Credit Bureau Development and Operation","Develop and operate a Credit Bureau",""],[1,"93","29","New Bank Building for NDBP","New bank building for NDBP to enable expansion of staff and services",""]],"73":[[1,"93","25","Online Land Registry Implementation","Research and implement an online land registry with assistance of ADB, IMF and WB",""],[1,"93","26","Legislation for Land, Bankruptcy, and Consumer Credit Protection","Introduce Legislation for Protection of Land, Bankruptcy, and Consumer Credit Protection",""]],"74":[[1,"97","1","NRFC Initiative Launch Support","in Palau could benefit from financial and technical support to launch similar NRFC initiatives with co-operatively owned vessels donated by Palau's international partners.",""],[1,"97","1","Inter-Agency Coordination for NRFC Initiatives","These types of initiatives require careful coordination between agencies, state governments, and the private sector.",""],[1,"97","2","BOFI Bouke-Ami Bait Net Acquisition and Testing","Given the past success of this \"bouke-ami\" baiting system, this style of net should be acquired for BOFI and tested to increase the baiting performance of the fishery.",""],[1,"97","3","Domestic Pelagic Fishing Industry Development","The PNMS Act includes provisions for a new domestic pelagic fishing industry to support the local market.",""],[1,"97","3","Local Fishing Fleet and Fisheries Infrastructure Development","Palau is exploring strategic partnerships to develop a local fishing fleet, establish a central fish auction market, build processing, and wharf facilities, and identify value-added products that can be developed from excess catch or by-catch.",""],[1,"97","3","Cold Chain and Dockside Fisheries Infrastructure Investment","Identified investment needs include cold chain storage for fishers, distributors, and buyers/end users, Fish Aggregating Devices (FADs), and dockside infrastructure.",""],[1,"97","4","Enhanced Engagement with International Partners and the PNA","Continued engagement with international partners and with the PNA is an immediate priority, including Palau taking a more active leadership role in scaling up marine spatial planning to the Micronesian region.",""],[1,"100","3","Cooperative Association Capacity-Building Support","Investment into cooperative associations, like the NRFC, particularly to build their business and entrepreneurial skills is needed.",""],[1,"100","3","Climate-Resilient Fisheries Infrastructure Development","Climate-resilient infrastructure (including updated docks) and cold chain infrastructure outside of urbanized areas will be needed in later years.",""],[1,"101","4","Interagency and Public-Private Coordination Mechanisms","Strengthen coordination mechanisms that allow for meaningful collaboration between agencies, state governments, and the private sector",""],[1,"101","6","Expanded Fisheries Dialogue Engagement","Expand engagement and participation in bilateral, regional, and international fisheries dialogues, with regional scaling",""],[1,"101","9","Aquaculture and Fisheries Supply Chain Infrastructure Investment","Invest in critical infrastructure in the aquaculture and fisheries supply chains, including research capacity to track impacts of climate change, and improve access to loans for private businesses",""],[1,"102","12","Capacity Development Programs","Appropriate capacity development programs are available.",""],[1,"102","12","Foreign Technical Assistance","Appropriate foreign technical assistance is available.",""],[1,"102","12","Infrastructure Feasibility Studies","Infrastructure feasibility studies are conducted.",""]],"75":[[1,"105","8","Telehealth Systems Development","Telehealth systems are being developed in partnership with Taiwan, Japan, New Zealand, and Australia for training, diagnosis, and treatment planning",""],[1,"105","9","Telehealth and Telemedicine Specialist Consultation System","A new telehealth/telemedicine equipment and system for specialist consultation with Shin Kong Hospital is being developed through a partnership with Taiwan",""],[1,"107","8","Patient-Centered Primary Care Realignment","A patient-centered approach is applied where all services are available at each visit to save time and be more effective in capturing diseases early.",""],[1,"107","8","Health Service Access Information Initiative","By 2026, all users know how to access services provided by MHHS.","MHHS"],[1,"107","8","Ministry-Wide Health Information System","Ministry-wide Health Information System is 100%.",""],[1,"107","8","Integrated Care System for IPV and MCH Populations","An integrated system of care will be instituted to support IPV and MCH populations.",""]],"76":[[1,"107","10","BNH Climate Resilience and Relocation Preparation","BNH will withstand the impacts of climate change pending relocation.",""]],"77":[[1,"107","8","Privatization Feasibility Assessment for Support Services","Feasibility assessment for privatizing support services will be completed. by 2024.",""]],"78":[[1,"108","6","Affordable Housing Supply Expansion","Find a solution to housing problems by making homes available at an affordable price and increasing the supply of housing.",""],[1,"108","8","Affordable Multi-Family Housing Construction Support","Support the construction of affordable multi-family dwellings to provide housing for short-term periods.",""],[1,"108","9","Affordable Housing Access for Citizens in Need","Provide access to affordable housing for citizens in need, prioritizing displaced citizens and first-time homeowners.",""],[1,"108","10","Public Land Housing Subdivision Investment","This will require investment in housing subdivisions on public lands.",""],[1,"109","3","Social Housing Support and Low-Interest Housing Loan Programme","Social housing support to those earning less than US$35,300 per annum is being provided by the Palau Housing Authority (PHA).",""],[1,"110","2","State Housing Subdivision Development","Every State has identified and or begun construction of housing subdivisions on public land to create more housing stock and attract more residents to come home.",""],[1,"110","2","Public-Private Housing Partnership Initiative","There have also been some private-public partnerships to create more housing.",""],[1,"112","8","Babeldaob Housing and Neighborhood Infrastructure Development","Infrastructure to support housing and neighborhood development is constructed each year in Babeldaob.",""],[1,"112","8","Babeldaob Pilot Housing Subdivision","Pilot housing subdivision is constructed in Babeldaob in 2026 in whichever state ready to proceed.",""],[1,"152","8","Housing Loan Facility through the Palau National Development Bank","The Republic of China is preparing a further housing loan of $15 million.",""]],"79":[[1,"108","7","Green Communities and Housing Subdivision Development","Coordinate the development of green communities, revival of old villages, and establishment of new housing subdivisions.",""],[1,"109","10","Culturally Sensitive Housing Development Planning","Any housing development needs to be cognizant of Palauan culture and should include, within the housing development plan, cultural facilities and, or restoration or upgrades to existing cultural sites.",""],[1,"110","6","Housing Policy Planning Process","A policy planning process is needed to raise awareness of housing issues and to identify coordinated strategies, policies, and actions to ensure that the housing needs of Palau's population are met.",""],[1,"111","1","Comprehensive Housing Assessment and Housing Policy","A comprehensive housing assessment is required, accompanied by a housing policy that identifies existing housing inventory, land suitable for housing including subdivisions, homes likely to be affected by climate change, and new building technologies thus ensuring Palauan access to safe and affordable homes.",""],[1,"111","1","Assessment of Multi-dwelling and Condominium Housing Options","This comprehensive assessment shall also explore and assess the applicability of multi-dwelling residences, condominiums, and other accommodations to alleviate the increasing gap between the demand for affordable housing and available supply.",""],[1,"112","8","Comprehensive Housing Needs Assessment","The comprehensive housing needs assessment is completed by the end of 2024.",""],[1,"112","8","National Housing Policy Approval","The comprehensive housing policy is completed and approved by the end of 2025.",""],[1,"112","8","PNCA 34 Review and Revision","PNCA 34 is reviewed and revised by the end of 2024.",""],[1,"112","8","State-Level Comprehensive Land Use Planning","Comprehensive land use plans are completed for all States by the end of 2025.",""],[1,"112","15","Comprehensive Housing Needs Assessment","Conduct a comprehensive housing needs assessment",""],[1,"112","18","Comprehensive Land Use Planning for All States","Complete comprehensive land use plans for all States (GEF 6)",""],[1,"112","20","Construction Materials and Methodologies Innovation Programme","Investigate and introduce new construction materials and methodologies, develop and implement education",""],[1,"112","21","Subdivision Planning Standards and Building Code Adoption","Prepare and adopt subdivision planning standards and building code",""],[1,"112","22","Construction Sector Professionalization Legislation","Increase levels of professionalism in the construction sector by developing and enacting legislation",""],[1,"112","24","Regional Infrastructure Development for Housing and Neighborhoods in Babeldaob","Develop regional infrastructure to support housing and neighborhood development in Babeldaob",""]],"80":[[1,"112","8","Climate-Impacted Housing Compensation Framework","Identify areas and homes that are likely to be impacted by climate change are identified, compensation legislation and policy developed, and lands suitable for housing subdivisions for impacted individuals identified by the end of 2025.",""],[1,"112","19","Policy to Protect Homes in Climate-Vulnerable Communities","Develop policy to protect homes in communities likely to be impacted by climate change",""]],"81":[[1,"112","8","Housing Materials and Methods Innovation Strategy","New construction materials and methodologies investigated, and an education strategy developed and implemented by the end of 2026.",""]],"82":[[1,"114","4","Belau Submarine Cable Corporation Core Network Development","Development of the Belau Submarine Cable Corporation, (BSCC) core network to eliminate single points of failure and deliver cost-effective high-speed connectivity",""],[1,"114","7","LTE Mobile Coverage Expansion","Mobile Coverage - 100% Long Term Evolution (LTE) also known as 4G population coverage by 2026.",""],[1,"114","9","Shared Core Infrastructure Planning and Resource Sharing","Shared Core Infrastructure - Maximise the value of core network infrastructure by collaborative planning and efficient sharing of resources.",""],[1,"114","14","Mobile Network Upgrade","Upgrade existing mobile network",""],[1,"114","15","Mobile Network Upgrade and Expansion","Upgrade and expand mobile network",""],[1,"115","5","ICT Services Expansion and Improvement","Expansion and improvement of ICT services by the two telecommunications SOE's (PNCC & BSCC), the Government and the private sector.",""],[1,"115","8","Off-Island Capacity Expansion via Babeldaob Loop","Provide extended access to off-island capacity to all operators via the Babeldaob Loop - to be in service by the end of 2023.",""],[1,"115","8","Off-Island Connectivity Resilience and Redundancy","Provide resiliency and redundancy of off-island capacity.",""],[1,"115","8","Koror and Airai 4G Network Upgrade","PNCC will upgrade its current 4G network in these areas by end 2023.",""],[1,"115","8","Nationwide 4G Coverage Expansion","Each mobile network operator to expand coverage to ensure that 4G coverage is extended to all of RoP by the end of 2026.",""],[1,"115","8","Universal Fixed-Line Broadband Rollout","Fast, reliable fixed-line broadband services to every home, business, and Govt. building throughout RoP by the end 2026.",""],[1,"115","8","Fiber to the Premises Rollout","in Palau through PNCC's Fiber to the Premises (FTTP) project.",""],[1,"115","10","BSCC Network Connection to Main Trunk via TPN","BSCC can connect to the main trunk through partner Trans-Pacific Networks (TPN) by Q2 2024.",""],[1,"115","10","Dual Copper and Fiber Network Rationalization","Time operating dual copper / fiber networks minimized to reduce cost",""],[1,"115","20","PNCC Mobile Network Replacement and Expansion","PNCC Mobile Network Replacement / Expansion c)",""],[1,"153","7","Technical Assistance for ICT Sector Operations and Infrastructure Planning","The World Bank has assisted Palau with ICT and oil and gas exploration and is planning to provide technical assistance to strengthen the operations of BSCC and PNCC to analyze additional ICT infrastructure needs with possible financing to use the international submarine cable more effectively, and to promote sector growth and development158.",""]],"83":[[1,"115","8","Government Services Portal","Increase ease of access to Government services via Government Services Portal.",""],[1,"115","8","Tax Online System","Increase the efficiency of tax collection process via Tax Online system.",""],[1,"115","8","National Cybersecurity Policy","Protect the data of citizens and businesses via National Cybersecurity Policy.",""],[1,"115","8","Cybercrimes Act","Provide regulation and framework for punishment of illegal activity online in Palau via Cybercrimes Act.",""],[1,"115","8","National Financial Management System Rollout","Full rollout of the National Financial Management System.",""],[1,"115","8","Customs Single Window Project","Increase efficiency, volume and value of customers collection via Customs Single Window Project (ASYCUDA)",""]],"84":[[1,"114","10","Industry-Level Disaster Preparedness Support","Preparedness - Industry-level support for Disaster Preparedness coordinated via NEMO.",""],[1,"114","10","Cell Broadcast Emergency Alert System","Cell Broadcast for all mobile operators by 2025 to enable rapid dissemination of critical safety information.",""]],"85":[[1,"116","4","Law Enforcement Infrastructure and Training Center Development","The MOJ is developing standard rules and operating procedures while building a centralized law enforcement complex.","MOJ"],[1,"116","4","BPS Central Rehabilitation and Public Service Hub","Specifically, the MOJ plans to rehabilitate the current Koror Jail and BPS administration building into \"BPS Central\", which will serve as a law enforcement center with officer training and support facilities where members of the public can seek a variety of police services in a secure, central location.","MOJ"],[1,"116","4","Regional Maritime Training Center Establishment","The MOJ also plans to establish a regional maritime training center within the existing compound of Marine Law in Malakal.","MOJ"],[1,"117","2","New Relocated Correctional Facility Construction","as part of the government's strategy, a plan for a new and relocated correctional facility began to be implemented.",""],[1,"117","10","Completion of the New Prison","The new prison needs to be completed but there is a lack of additional funding due to piecemeal appropriations.",""],[1,"118","6","Prison Completion Capital Investment","Additional capital to complete the new prison.",""],[1,"119","8","Repair and Replacement of Ministry of Justice Offices and Facilities","MOJ offices and facilities are either repaired or replaced to provide an optimum work environment by 2025.","MOJ"],[1,"119","22","Ngchesar New Prison Construction and Furnishing","Complete construction of and furnish new Prison in Ngchesar",""],[1,"146","16","New Prison Construction and Furnishing in Ngchesar","Complete construction of and furnishings for the new Prison in Ngchesar",""]],"86":[[1,"117","12","K9 Narcotics Detection Program Funding","The current K9 Program needs funding to enable stronger detection of narcotics at our air and seaports as well as postal services.",""],[1,"117","14","Police Service Strengthening and Justice Efficiency Improvement","The government intends to improve the police coverage, staffing, management, technology integration, and overall efficiency and effectiveness of carrying out justice in the Republic from proactive intervention and community policing to investigations, case management,",""],[1,"118","1","Crime Prosecution Capacity Strengthening","and prosecution of crime through adequate and ongoing training and education, standardized investigation and reporting processes, and close partnerships within MOJ.","MOJ"],[1,"118","7","Parole Officers Program","Establish a parole officers' program to ensure the rehabilitation of inmates and to reduce recidivism.",""],[1,"118","8","K9 Program Strengthening","Strengthening of the K9 Program",""],[1,"118","10","CCTV Coverage Expansion in Key Areas","CCTV coverage for key areas that do not have CCTVs, especially in Koror and Airai",""],[1,"119","8","Police Service Improvement and Accountability Measures","Capture intake (reports), investigations, and prosecution data and create and make statistics public to maintain transparency and public accountability.",""],[1,"119","8","Port Inspection and K9 Handler Capacity Expansion","Increase inspections and surveillance of our ports through cross-utilization of our K9 program and to increase the number of officers trained as K9 Handlers.",""],[1,"119","8","Corrections Division and Rehabilitation Program Development","Having a suitable Division of Corrections in place with proper rehab programs in place.",""]],"87":[[1,"118","3","Babeldaob Emergency Services Substation Expansion","Expanding substations to include both police units and fire and ambulatory services to ensure consistent response times in all parts of Babeldaob, including the provision of vehicles and equipment.",""],[1,"118","4","Fire Tanker Replacement and Expansion","Additional fire tankers in Koror and Babeldaob to replace old fire engines.",""],[1,"118","5","Fire Hydrant System Upgrade","The fire hydrant system needs to be updated to ensure faster refill and response time.",""]],"88":[[1,"120","1","Comprehensive Waste Management System with 3R+Return Policy","developing and implementing a comprehensive waste management system with the 3R+Return Policy by employing sustainable solutions consistent with traditional and cultural values.",""],[1,"120","4","State Waste Collection System from Segregation Stations","Recently, the Koror State Government (KSG) started implementing a new system for collecting waste from segregation stations.",""],[1,"121","4","Outsourced Waste Collection and Disposal Contract for Babeldaob States","BPW is in the process of outsourcing the waste collection service for Babeldaob States.",""],[1,"121","5","Revolving Fund for Waste Collection and Solid Waste Management","A revolving fund finances the Babeldaob waste collection service.",""],[1,"121","8","M-Dock Landfill Operation and Maintenance","Operation and maintenance of M-Dock Landfill.",""],[1,"122","10","Solid Waste Collection Improvement","Solid waste collection is improved in 10 States of Babeldaob Island and in Koror.",""],[1,"122","11","Landfill Transition to a New Site","The ongoing transition from the M-dock landfill to a new landfill.",""],[1,"123","1","Babeldaob States Waste Collection Service Contract","A service Contract for the Babeldaob States Waste Collection Service is pending.",""],[1,"123","2","Solid Waste Disposal Facilities and Best Practices Upgrade","The government will gradually introduce state-of-the-art facilities and best practices to dispose of solid wastes and thereby promote improved health and preserve the natural environment.",""],[1,"152","3","National Landfill Reconstruction","Reconstruction of the national landfill",""]],"89":[[1,"121","5","Recycling Fund for Solid Waste Management","Revenue from a recycling fund is approximately $360,000 annually.",""],[1,"121","6","Waste Segregation and Recycling Improvement","Improving waste management through segregation and recycling (to reduce inputs to dumps) is an immediate priority, and restoration, mitigation, and, or capping of dumps is a medium-term priority.",""],[1,"122","2","Scrap Metal Collection and Recycling Contract","BPW has a contract (Contract No. 12-029) with Palau Waste Collection to collect all scrap metal entering the M-dock landfill for recycling purposes.","BPW"],[1,"122","3","Recycling Program","· Recycling Program (RPPL 7-24).",""],[1,"122","4","Waste Management Awareness Programs","Awareness programs are conducted throughout the year to promote the 3Rs, waste segregation, and the importance of best waste management practices.",""],[1,"122","6","Zero Waste Society Promotion Project","International Center Environmental Technology Transfer (ICETT) \"project of working together with the government and the citizens for zero waste society promotion in the Republic of Palau\".",""],[1,"122","7","JPRISM II Solid Waste Management Cooperation Project","Japanese Technical Cooperation Project for Promotion of Regional Initiatives on Solid Waste Management in Pacific Island Countries Phase II (JPRISM II).",""],[1,"122","9","3R Solid Waste Management Promotion","Good practices of solid waste management, that is \"3R\" are promoted in the country and the region.",""],[1,"122","13","Scrap Metal and Beverage Container Recycling Contract","Service Contract No. 12-029 with Palau Waste Collection to collect all scrap metal entering the M-dock landfill for recycling purposes.",""],[1,"122","15","Beverage Container Redemption Center Operation Agreement","MOU with KSG to operate as an initial redemption center under the Beverage Container Recycling Regulations (RPPL 7-24).",""],[1,"124","6","Scrap Metal Storage Area Establishment","Scrap metal storage area established by FY25.",""],[1,"124","6","Tipping Fee System Implementation","Tipping Fee system implemented by FY25.",""],[1,"124","6","Private Recycler Incentive Scheme","Private company recyclers incentives established by FY26.",""],[1,"124","6","Recycling Programme Expansion","Recycling program expanded by FY24.",""],[1,"124","6","Advance Recovery Fee and Deposit Scheme","Advance Recovery Fee & Deposit (ARFD) established by FY25.",""],[1,"124","14","Designated Scrap Metal Recycling Area Near National Landfill","Identify a designated area near the National landfill-Aimeliik for a private scrap metal recycler for the purpose of scrap metal collection, treatment, and export at no cost to the government.",""],[1,"124","15","National Landfill Tipping Fee System","Establish a Tipping Fee system at the National Landfill to support the Operations and Maintenance of the landfill.",""],[1,"124","16","Private Company Recycler Incentive Scheme","Strengthen private company recyclers by providing incentives such as tax breaks.",""],[1,"124","17","Expansion of Recycling Program to Non-Beverage Containers","Expand recycling program to include non- beverage containers",""],[1,"124","19","Advance Recovery Fee and Deposit Scheme","Establish Advance Recovery Fee & Deposit (ARFD) towards sound material cycle society is developed and a legal framework for at least one problematic waste stream is developed.",""]],"90":[[1,"121","6","Dump Restoration, Mitigation, and Capping","Improving waste management through segregation and recycling (to reduce inputs to dumps) is an immediate priority, and restoration, mitigation, and, or capping of dumps is a medium-term priority.",""],[1,"121","6","Marine Debris Management","Managing the flow of marine debris is a medium- to long-term priority for communities.",""],[1,"123","3","Closure and Rehabilitation of Disused Waste Disposal Sites","With the construction of the new national landfill in Aimeliik State the older, now disused waste disposal sites need to be closed and the land rehabilitated and returned to commercial or agricultural use, and",""],[1,"124","6","Dump Site Closure Programme","Half of dump sites closed by end of FY27.",""]],"91":[[1,"123","4","Waste-to-Energy Technology Deployment","Waste-to-Energy technology would significantly reduce the volume of waste disposed at the landfill and at the same time produce usable energy.",""]],"92":[[1,"127","2","Palauan Arts and Cultural Revival Initiative","There also needs to be a revival of Palauan arts and culture.",""],[1,"127","2","Cultural Tourism Development Initiative","Most States' master plans want to establish cultural tourism.",""],[1,"127","2","Cultural Curriculum and Community Skills Transmission","Not only will this involve the Historic Preservation Office with historical registered sites but also the school system to establish a cultural learning part of the curriculum and the community in passing hands-on skills and knowledge.","Historic Preservation Office"],[1,"127","9","Participatory Policy Dissemination and Consultation Program","A program of participatory workshops, other meetings, and policy dissemination.",""],[1,"127","11","Tourism Destination Development for Waterfalls and Park","The development of Ngeremiengul waterfall, Ngchesar Waterfall, and Ngiwal Park as tourist destinations.",""],[1,"128","8","Annual Palauan Arts and Culture Events","At least one Palauan arts and culture event in each State, each year from FY 25 to FY 27.",""],[1,"128","10","Participatory Tourism Knowledge Dissemination","Participatory processes support the widespread dissemination of new tourism knowledge.",""],[1,"131","7","Private-Sector Tourism Product Development and Marketing Support","Private-sector tourism product development and marketing continue to support the restoration of the tourism industry.",""]],"93":[[1,"128","3","Tourism Recovery and Value-Added Visitor Strategy","Recover the number of tourists to 150,000 with every visitor bringing added value to the environment, society, culture, governance, and economy of Palau by the end of FY 2027.",""]],"94":[[1,"129","1","Air Transport Service Maintenance and Certification Programme","This includes maintaining our certification with continuous training for Aircraft Rescue and Fire Fighting, Airport Police, Automatic Flight Information Service Unit, Navigational Aide Technicians, and Airfield and Facilities Maintenance Personnel.",""],[1,"130","2","ICAO SARPs Compliance Improvement","Palau needs to continue to work towards addressing the International and Civil Aviation Organization (ICAO) SARPS (Standards and Recommended Practices) based on the 2010 ICAO audit.",""],[1,"130","5","Airfield Operations and Maintenance Support","Support the operation and maintenance of Angaur and Peleliu Airfields.",""],[1,"130","5","ARFF and Airport Police Training and Recertification","Finance basic training and recertification for ARFF and Airport Police to maintain safety and security standards.",""],[1,"130","6","Airport Rescue Firefighting Building Refurbishment","Refurbish, renovate and repair the Airport Rescue Firefighting building.",""],[1,"130","7","Rescue Equipment and Firefighting Gear Procurement","Acquire new rescue equipment and firefighting gear.",""],[1,"130","8","VHF Radio Procurement","Acquire a new VHF base and handheld radios.",""],[1,"130","9","Air Service Facilities and Airport Personnel Certification","To plan for and build air service facilities, and certification of airport personnel to maintain the safety and regulatory environment as the demand for air services increases.",""],[1,"131","8","Airport Firefighting and Security Capacity Strengthening","Recertification of ARFF Training, Basic Training, and Continuous Recruitment Recertification of Airport Police Live Fire Training and Execution Security Program Assessment Completion of Personnel Leadership Training Completion of ACM, AEP, WHMP, and ALP Coordination and Cooperation on Joint Use Agreement with the US",""]],"95":[[1,"130","3","Peleliu and Angaur Airfield Safety Upgrading","The Peleliu and Angaur airfields need to be developed to meet basic safety standards.",""],[1,"130","14","Peleliu and Angaur Airfields Development for Runway Safety","Peleliu and Angaur Airfields need to be developed to maintain runway safety measures.",""],[1,"130","15","Airport Runway and Taxiway Surface Resealing","The international airport's existing runway and taxiways will require a surface reseal during the period of the PDP.",""],[1,"130","16","International Airport Renovation and Expansion Project","a project involving major renovations to the international airport, including additional new gates with an estimated cost of $40 million funded by JICA/JBIC/SMBC is currently under implementation",""],[1,"130","16","Airport Customs Modernization Expansion","A proposal to expand the scope of this project by including X-Ray equipment and a computerized Customs management system (ASYCUDA) at a cost of $5 million, is also currently under consideration",""],[1,"130","17","Aircraft Registry Establishment through Legislation","· Establish Aircraft Registry through Legislation",""],[1,"131","8","Air Transport Service Expansion","Increasing Air Transport Service with AP Region",""],[1,"131","8","Runway Extension for Large Aircraft","Extension of Runway to meet large aircraft",""],[1,"131","21","Peleliu and Angaur Airfields Development","Develop Peleliu and Angaur Airfields",""],[1,"131","22","International Airport Runway and Taxiway Resealing","Reseal international airport's runway and taxiways",""],[1,"152","4","Palau International Airport Renovation, Expansion, and Operation","Renovation, expansion, and operation of Palau International Airport",""]],"96":[[1,"132","6","Roads, Causeways, and Bridges Network Expansion","To slowly build up the roads, causeways, and bridges network and associated safety and regulatory environment as the demand for land transport increases.",""],[1,"133","2","Koror-Airai Road Repairs Design","Desing of Koror-Airai road repairs",""],[1,"133","4","State Road Paving and Connectivity Improvement","Paving the roads from each state that connect to the Compact Road or to communities within a state will remain a priority for the duration of the plan",""],[1,"133","5","Minato Bridge Preparatory Study and New Bridge Construction","Minato Bridge Preparatory Study and construction of a new bridge",""],[1,"133","7","Pedestrian Walkway Rehabilitation and Construction","Rehabilitate or build new pedestrian walkways in Koror.",""],[1,"133","8","Periodic Road Repair Programme","Periodic repair of random road areas to prevent premature pavement impairment",""],[1,"134","5","Rural Road Improvement and Paving Programme","All roads in rural areas of Babeldaob connecting to the Compact Road are improved with reinforced Portland cement concrete.",""],[1,"134","5","Interstate Village Road Paving Programme","All interstate roads connecting villages within states are paved as mentioned above.",""],[1,"134","5","Bridge and Culvert Renewal Programme","Main bridges and culverts on causeways are renewed/improved to ensure vehicular traffic safety and extended service life of infrastructure.",""],[1,"152","7","Japan-Palau Friendship Bridge Construction","Construction of the Japan-Palau Friendship Bridge",""]],"97":[[1,"133","3","Climate-Proofing of Low-Lying Roads and Causeways","Climate-proofing of low-lying roads and causeways.",""],[1,"133","6","Culvert Replacement on Malakal and Meyuns Causeways","Replacement of culverts on Malakal and Meyuns causeways",""]],"98":[[1,"133","11","Public Transportation Investment Options Review","the government will also examine options to invest in public transportation, with the objective of reducing congestion and CO2 emissions.",""]],"99":[[1,"133","12","Technical Training for Development Planning and Inspection","Technical training (in person and virtual) in development planning, construction inspection, maintenance inspections",""],[1,"133","13","Technical Maintenance Training","Technical training on maintenance",""],[1,"134","8","Project Documentation and Supplemental Project Details Preparation","Project Documentation and Supplemental Project Details write-up and submission to funding agencies.",""],[1,"134","8","Project Inception and Delivery Arrangement Planning","Project inception planning including the determination of whether to outsource projects, perform them in-house or perform thru Force Account Agreements with State Governments.",""],[1,"134","8","Project Scope and Bill of Quantities Development","Development of project scope of works and bill of quantities needed for procurement purposes or in-house implementation or force account.",""],[1,"134","8","Construction Management and Project Handover","Provide construction management.",""]],"100":[[1,"137","2","Marine Navigation Aids Rehabilitation and Replacement","Through grant funding assistance from partner countries, the Bureau of Marine Transportation has been able to replace all floating aids and is undertaking the rehabilitation of 85 beacon markers.",""],[1,"137","6","Navigation Aids and Waterway Marking","The government will also continue to mark the entrances of all state waterways with lighted aids and mark all risks to navigation",""],[1,"137","10","West Pass Range Marker Replacement","Replace two sets of range markers in West Pass",""],[1,"137","11","Malakal Harbor Light Aid Replacement","Replace light aid in Malakal Harbor",""],[1,"137","12","East Pass Light Aid Extension","Extend light aid in front of East Pass",""],[1,"137","13","State Waterway Beacon Installation","Install 115 new beacons in state waterways",""],[1,"138","21","Replacement and Expansion of Light Aids and New Beacon Installation","Replace and extend light aids and place new beacons",""]],"101":[[1,"137","6","Government-Operated Inter-Island Marine Transport Service","The government intends to increase its role in the marine transport sector to improve marine transport services by (i) replacing a less efficient private sector fleet of small vessels servicing the islands with one larger government-owned and operated ship",""],[1,"137","6","Drydock Feasibility Assessment","investigating the potential viability of investing in a drydock",""],[1,"137","6","Malakal Port Rehabilitation and Expansion","rehabilitating the existing port in Malakal to increase the land area by acquiring the adjacent fisheries dock, and thereby create a mechanism for seafarer training",""],[1,"137","7","Government Vessel Feasibility Study and Investment","Feasibility study followed by the investment and operation of a government vessel",""],[1,"137","8","Dry-dock Facility Feasibility Study and Construction","Feasibility study followed by the construction of a Dry-dock Facility",""],[1,"137","9","Malakal Commercial Port Expansion and Rehabilitation","Feasibility study followed by the expansion and Rehabilitation of Malakal Commercial Port",""],[1,"138","5","Government-Owned Maritime Transport Service Upgrade","Increased government role in the maritime transport sector to improve maritime transport services by (i) replacing a less efficient private sector fleet of small vessels servicing the islands with one larger government-owned and operated ship, thereby creating a mechanism for seafarer training, and maintaining navigation aids.",""],[1,"138","5","Palau Drydock Development","(ii) a Palau drydock supplying a lower cost service than existing domestic and Philippine drydocks.",""],[1,"138","5","Malakal Port Rehabilitation and Expansion","rehabilitating the existing port in Malakal to increase the land area by acquiring adjacent fisheries dock, as indicated by a) stabilized freight rates as the port will be able to handle larger and more cost-efficient vessels, and b) an increase in luxury yacht visits.",""],[1,"138","8","Government-Owned Vessel Operations","The government-owned and operated vessel commences operation and provides increased maritime transport services to all islands at a lower cost than previous operations.",""],[1,"138","8","Government-Owned Drydock Operations","The government-owned (and possibly private sector- operated) drydock commences operation and provides services at a lower cost.",""],[1,"138","8","Extended Malakal Port Operations","Extended Malakal port provides increased port services at a lower cost than previous operations.",""]],"102":[[1,"140","3","Land Use Planning and Zoning for Sediment Reduction","Implementation of land use planning and zoning to reduce future sediment inputs is an immediate priority.",""],[1,"140","3","Erosion Control, Tree Planting, and Land Cover Rehabilitation Programme","Institutionalizing a program of erosion control, tree planting, or land cover rehabilitation (for which there is proof of concept) is also an immediate priority.",""]],"103":[[1,"142","4","Water and Sewerage Tariff Reform","A framework of tariffs and tariff increases to achieve full cost recovery has been agreed upon and is being implemented.",""],[1,"142","7","Water Management Legislative and Regulatory Reform","The government seeks to further amend legislation and regulations in support of improved water management.",""],[1,"142","7","Water Infrastructure Investment and Tariff Reform","The government is investing in new plants and gradually raising tariffs to reduce subsidies, adopting new, more appropriate ownership, and has taken action to strengthen water and sewer management and to otherwise seek to improve operational efficiencies and effectiveness.",""],[1,"150","1","PPUC Corporate Governance and Financial Management Strengthening","The loan to PPUC will strengthen the utility's corporate governance and financial management to ensure sustainable service delivery.",""],[1,"153","1","Utility and Public Sector Performance Support","ADB is helping improve utility and public sector performance alongside infrastructure works.",""],[1,"153","4","Palau Public Utilities Corporation Governance and Financial Management Strengthening","The loan to PPUC will strengthen the utility's corporate governance and financial management to ensure sustainable service delivery.",""]],"104":[[1,"142","12","Water Desalination Plant Rehabilitation","The rehabilitation of water desalination plants",""],[1,"142","14","Chemical Storage Room Construction","Construction of an additional chemical storage room with AC that can store up to at least 6 months' worth of supplies.",""],[1,"143","1","Ngerikiil Dam Rehabilitation and Capacity Expansion","Raise the existing Ngerikiil Dam Weir by 2ft and re-construct the Ngerikiil Dam Walls to stop leakage and increase volume capacity.",""],[1,"143","2","Distribution Storage Tank Refurbishment","Refurbishing of the Distribution Storage Tanks in Airai, Ngermid, Ngerkesoal, and Ngerkebesang.",""],[1,"143","7","Water Quality Monitoring and Sanitation Training","Water quality monitoring and sanitation training.",""],[1,"143","9","Melekeok Treatment Plant Renovation and Expansion","The renovation and expansion of the Melekeok treatment plant",""],[1,"143","12","Long-Term Water Resource and Chemical Management Investments","Additional longer-term investments will be needed to manage chemicals and determine water-sharing regimes, especially as agriculture expands and if irrigation places a demand on the water during times of drought.",""],[1,"144","23","Ngerikiil Dam Weir Raising and Dam Wall Reconstruction","Raise Ngerikiil Dam Weir by 2ft and reconstruct Dam Walls",""],[1,"144","24","Distribution Storage Tank Refurbishment","Refurbish the Distribution Storage Tanks - Airai, Ngermid, Ngerkesoaol, and Ngerkebesang",""],[1,"146","19","Distribution Storage Tank Refurbishment","III.5 Refurbish the Distribution Storage Tanks - Airai, Ngermid, Ngerkesoaol, and Ngerkebesang",""],[1,"147","3","Ngerikiil Dam Weir Raising and Dam Wall Reconstruction","Raise Ngerikiil Dam Weir by 2ft and reconstruct Dam Walls",""]],"105":[[1,"145","1","Capital Expenditure Approval and Prioritization Process","The Palau NIIP138 adopted a 5-stage process of infrastructure approval that can now be applied to all capital expenditures: (i) compile a long list of all proposed capital expenditures, (ii) assess each proposal's readiness for appraisal, (iii) approve the Multi- Criteria Analysis (MCA) criteria, (iv) use the MCA to score proposals that are ready for appraisal and prioritize them, and (v) seek funding.",""],[1,"145","3","CAPEX Committee Capital Expenditure Clearance Mechanism","all capital expenditure should first be cleared by a \"CAPEX Committee\"","the Attorney General's Office | the Ministry of Finance | the Office of Human Resources | the Ministry of Public Infrastructure and Industries | the Ministries of Health and Education | the Ministry of Agriculture, Fisheries and the Environment | the Bureau of Land and Survey"],[1,"146","2","Capital Expenditure Prioritization Framework","Capital expenditures are prioritized regardless of funding source; that is, whether they are to be funded from domestic revenues or possibly donor or development partner financed.",""],[1,"146","2","MCA Guidance Notes Publication","MCA guidance notes are also available on the MOF website.","MOF"]],"106":[[1,"147","8","Grid-Forming Battery Installation near Koror","Installation of a grid forming battery near Koror",""]],"107":[[1,"152","11","Programmatic Climate Change Approach","It introduces new priorities for a programmatic approach to climate change, longer-term capacity",""],[1,"153","3","Pacific Disaster Resilience Program Phase 3 Contingent Financing","Phase 3 of ADB's Pacific Disaster Resilience Program will provide $20 million in disaster-contingent financing for recovery and reconstruction following future natural hazards or health emergencies",""],[1,"153","5","UN Palau Joint Country Action Plan","The 2021 UN Palau Joint Country Action Plan is assisting Palau with (i) climate change, disaster resilience, and environmental protection; (ii) gender equality; (iii) sustainable and inclusive economic empowerment; (iv) equitable basic services; (v) governance and community engagement; and (vi) human rights.",""]],"108":[[1,"153","4","Public Financial Management and Fiscal Risk Reduction Support","The RISES Program has assisted Palau in strengthening policy and legislative frameworks for public financial management, reducing fiscal risks linked to weak public sector asset management, and supporting private sector development.",""]],"109":[[1,"153","4","Information and Communication Technology, Sanitation, and Energy Projects","Other ongoing projects in Palau are in information and communication technology, sanitation, and energy.",""]],"110":[[1,"152","6","Palau International Coral Reef Research Center Construction","Construction of the Palau International Coral Reef Research Center",""],[1,"154","1","Blue Prosperity Plan Implementation Support","currently processing an investment project and technical assistance in support of the implementation of the Blue Prosperity Plan for approval late 2024.",""]],"111":[[1,"154","2","Mobilization of Multilateral Climate Change Assistance","ensuring greater assistance from multilateral climate change schemes might help to cope with the substantial adaptation cost to prepare for natural disasters and climate change and to finance any proposals for wave energy, solar energy, and other renewable energy projects.",""]],"112":[[1,"154","3","Sustainable and Inclusive Socio-Economic Recovery Support","In the wake of the COVID-19 crisis, the EU will focus on creating the conditions for a sustainable and inclusive socio-economic recovery and will work actively with its partners in the following seven areas: (i) Sustainable and inclusive prosperity; (ii) Green transition; (iii) Ocean governance; (iv) Digital governance and partnerships; (v) Connectivity; (vi) Security and defense; and (vii) Human security.",""],[1,"154","4","Business Environment Strengthening through PPPs, Transparency, and Credit Access","The Pacific Private Sector Development Initiative is strengthening the business environment by supporting PPPs, increased transparency, and improved access to credit.",""]],"113":[[1,"155","7","Chemical Storage Room Construction and Life Cycle Management Improvement","Construction of additional Chemical Storage Room and improved Life Cycle management",""]],"114":[[1,"155","13","New Prison Construction and Furnishing in Ngchesar","Complete construction of and furnishings for the new Prison in Ngchesar",""]],"115":[[1,"157","1","Sector Performance Monitoring and Funding Framework Updates","PDP progress will be annually monitored at the sector level when each sector performance monitoring and funding framework is updated every April to June in preparation for annual budget negotiations.",""],[1,"157","2","End-of-Plan Development Evaluation","An end of PDP evaluation will be prepared and presented at the Development Symposium to be held in November 2026.",""]]}});